1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
﻿*I've always liked stargazing, but what really got me invested in space was my older cousin, Seiji. He's an even bigger space nut than I am, if that can be believed.*

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
*When I was younger, Seiji used to take me hiking, so we could look up at the stars.*

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:27,000
*He gave me a collapsible telescope for my twelfth birthday. It was a pretty cheap telescope, and it wasn't all that powerful, but I cherished it.*

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
*Those days I spent with my cousin, out in the sticks, were truly precious.*

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
*A lot of time has passed since then, though, and I'm not the wide-eyed, easily-impressed little kid I used to be.*

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,000
*I'm nineteen, and I've since moved from the countryside to attend university in Tokyo.*

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:55,000
*I'm studying physics, thanks to my childhood fascination with the stars, and I have dreams of becoming a researcher when I graduate.*

8
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000
*I'd love to work for JAXA one day, and oversee satellites as they're launched into orbit...*

9
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,000
*But I'm getting ahead of myself.*

10
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:14,000
*Nothing's certain in life. It's best to focus on the here and the now. I don't want to end up disappointed, even if I'm doing all in my power to make my dreams come true.*

11
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
*I'll take things one step at a time.*

12
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:24,000
*Since I'd lived out in the sticks all my life, moving to Tokyo was, initially, a huge culture shock.*

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:31,000
*Tokyo's busy 24/7, with a huge amount of buildings, and it's wreathed in perpetually flickering lights.*

14
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:45,000
*I live in a run-down apartment block with a bunch of other guys around my age. I'm situated on the third floor, in a teeny room with a tatami floor that overlooks a parking lot and a bunch of Chinese restaurants.*

15
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:54,000
*The smell of frying beef loin and pork belly wafts through my window every evening without fail, which ensures I always go to sleep hungry.*

16
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:04,000
*I live in a pretty busy area, and cars go by every hour of the day. In the beginning, their constant humming used to bother me, but I've gotten used to it.*

17
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,000
*I've been in Tokyo for eight months now, and the regular hustle and bustle has become old hat.*

18
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:19,000
*My passion for space hasn't waned during these months, but I've not had many opportunities to put the telescope Seiji gave me to good use.*

19
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:27,000
*I still have it, old and worn though it is, but Tokyo's night skies are so crowded it's hard to get a good view of the stars.*

20
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:33,000
*There's too much light pollution to contend with - not to mention all the actual pollution.*

21
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,000
*The skies here are never as clear as they are back home.*

22
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
*That's the one thing I miss about the countryside.*

23
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:52,000
*I wasn't too cut up about leaving my childhood home, on account of its critical lack of decent shops and the awful public transport, but the clear night skies were something special.*

24
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
*I think I took them for granted.*

25
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:59,000
*I had no idea, before I left for Tokyo, what I'd be saying goodbye to.*

26
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:08,000
*It's not all doom and gloom, though. I can't stargaze as often as I'd like, but I do have occasional opportunities to peruse the night sky.*

27
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:15,000
*My university has a club devoted solely for stargazing, which - of course - I signed up for in a snap.*

28
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:26,000
*I figured that I, alongside my new club members, would be making regular trips out to the countryside, to camp beneath the stars, like I did with Seiji in my childhood...*

29
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:33,000
*But my dreams of camaraderie under the stars were doused when the reality of the situation hit me.*

30
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:38,000
*My university's astronomy club is, to put it politely, somewhat lacking...*

31
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:42,000
*And, to put it rather less politely, it's almost a non-entity.*

32
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:48,000
*I'm surprised it's still running, given its list of members stops short at a measly two.*

33
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:57,000
*There's the club leader, a cheery girl called Akasaka Hiyori, one year my senior, and me, Takagi Haru, and that's it. The end. C'est fini.*

34
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,000
*We're the only members of the astronomy club.*

35
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
*I'm stuck dealing with Hiyori all alone, and boy, is she a lot to deal with. For example...*

36
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Hiyori: "Hey, Haru! It's good to see you again this morning!"

37
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Hiyori: "Glomp!"

38
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Haru: "Aaah...!"

39
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:17,000
*I start, surprised, as I feel a soft sensation pushed up against my arm.*

40
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:25,000
*I probably shouldn't be as surprised as I am, given how often this scene plays out, but it shocks me all the same.*

41
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:29,000
*I've only just stepped outside, and I'm already being assaulted.*

42
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Hiyori: "How are you, Haru? Are you doing well?"

43
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Hiyori: "I hope you've been looking after yourself! It's been chilly lately, hasn't it?"

44
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Hiyori: "You ought to make sure you wrap up warm - and make sure you eat a lot of nutritious food, too!"

45
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:49,000
*Hiyori starts babbling nineteen to the dozen, as she always does.*

46
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:55,000
*It's hard to get any words in when this girl is around - but I have to at least make an effort.*

47
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Haru: "Hey, Hiyori..."

48
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:06,000
*I try to wrench my arm free of Hiyori's pincer-like grasp, to little avail. She's clinging to me hard, as though she's afraid I might disappear...*

49
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:10,000
*Which, if I'm being fair, wouldn't be a wholly baseless fear.*

50
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,000
*I do find Hiyori's company quite overwhelming.*

51
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:23,000
*She's more touchy-feely than any girl I've ever met before (not that I know all that many girls), and we haven't known one another all that long.*

52
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:26,000
*It's not like we're childhood friends or anything.*

53
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,000
*She has no sense of boundaries whatsoever.*

54
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,000
*To be honest, I find Hiyori's clinginess kind of...*

55
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Hiyori: "But Haru!"

56
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
*Hiyori pouts, her wide eyes boring into my own.*

57
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:46,000
*Hiyori looks pretty plain, with her bobbed brown hair and her brown eyes, but in terms of personality, she really is out there.*

58
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
*Is she overcompensating for her average looks?*

59
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:53,000
*I've often pondered this, during the months I've known her...*

60
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:57,000
*But that's a mean thought, so I'll keep it to myself.*

61
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Hiyori: "I have to cling to you, to warm you up! It's a cold day, and - oh!"

62
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:06,000
*Hiyori squeezes my hand between her own, then squeaks in alarm.*

63
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Hiyori: "Why don't you wear gloves? The weather reporter said it was below zero!"

64
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Haru: "I-It's alright. I used to live in the countryside. It got even colder there. I'm used to it."

65
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Hiyori: "Wow, that's so cool. You always act so tough..."

66
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:32,000
*Hiyori giggles, then snuggles even closer to me. She lets go of my hand (thank goodness), but her fingers are quick to coil once more around my arm.*

67
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:38,000
*She pulls my body towards hers, presses her cheek to the curve of my shoulder, then beams.*

68
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Hiyori: "But you don't need to act tough around me! We are friends, after all!"

69
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Hiyori: "If you are cold, just say the word, and I'll warm you up in a snap!"

70
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Hiyori: "My body temperature is a little higher than your average person's..."

71
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Hiyori: "Though, that should be expected, given I'm not an average person at all!"

72
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Hiyori: "You should already know that by this point, though, so I won't bore you with the details!"

73
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
Haru: "Yeah, uh... Thanks..."

74
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:17,000
*Hiyori might look completely normal to an outsider, but she maintains (quite forcefully, in fact) that she is not, in fact, an ordinary girl.*

75
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:20,000
*She believes, instead, that she's an alien.*

76
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:28,000
*I was pretty unnerved when Hiyori first told me about this insane theory - and, to be honest, I'm still unnerved.*

77
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:35,000
*I thought about quitting the astronomy club when she dropped that bombshell, but I wasn't able to do it.*

78
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:42,000
*I love stargazing too much to pass it up, and while Hiyori is strange, I don't think she means any ill.*

79
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:49,000
*She's a nice girl, really - if a bit too attentive to my needs - and I definitely don't dislike her.*

80
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:56,000
*If it weren't for me, the astronomy club would have only one member, and it would be forced to disband.*

81
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:04,000
*I know how much her club means to Hiyori. I'd hate to be the harbinger of its demise, even if it is on its last legs.*

82
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:11,000
*I'm willing to tough out Hiyori's... uh, Hiyori-ness, at least until the end of the semester, but...*

83
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:20,000
Koichi: "Hey, Haru! Can you maybe, like, not flirt with your girlfriend so early in the morning? You're going to make me puke, man!"

84
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Daigo: "That's right! You don't have to show off like that! Are you trying to rub it in?!"

85
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Kosuke: "Guys with girlfriends are the worst. They think they're all that, just because they have a bit more luck than us."

86
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:38,000
Kosuke: "Normies really are the worst! They should all drop dead!"

87
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Haru: "Geez..."

88
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:46,000
*I sigh. It's such a cold day my breath, as it escapes my mouth, turns white and gauzy, like steam.*

89
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:53,000
*I was hoping to steer Hiyori away from the apartment before my housemates woke up, but I'm all out of luck.*

90
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
*I've already been spotted.*

91
00:08:55,000 --> 00:09:02,000
*Koichi is glaring at me like he wants to punch a hole through my face, and Kosuke just spat on the sidewalk.*

92
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,000
*How charming – not.*

93
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:07,000
*And Kosuke wonders why he doesn't have a girlfriend...*

94
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:11,000
*Not that I'm dating Hiyori, for all she clings to me.*

95
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Hiyori: "Oh, hi there, Haru's housemates!"

96
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:19,000
*Heedless of my housemates' death glares, Hiyori shoots them a cheery smile.*

97
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
Hiyori: "It's nice to see you!"

98
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:31,000
Hiyori: "Make sure you wrap up warm, alright? It's very cold! I'd hate for you to get sick - and I'd hate it even more if you gave my dear Haru pneumonia!"

99
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Haru: "H-Hey, guys."

100
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:40,000
*I wave to my housemates with my free hand, then try to extricate myself from both Hiyori and this awkward misunderstanding.*

101
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Haru: "I think you've got the wrong idea. Hiyori and I aren't dating-"

102
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,000
*I begin, but Kosuke cuts me off.*

103
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:53,000
Kosuke: "Like hell you aren't! What girl clings to a guy if she doesn't have a thing for him?!"

104
00:09:53,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Kosuke: "I'm not stupid, you know? I can see what's going on! This girl totally has the hots for you!"

105
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Daigo: "Kosuke's right! It's so obvious! You can't trick us with that "we're not dating" bullcrap!"

106
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:11,000
Daigo: "She only deigns to look at us because we live with you!"

107
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:19,000
Koichi: "I don't care one way or the other if you want to flirt, but don't, like, do it right in front of us, man. It's rude."

108
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Haru: "N-No, we're really not dating..."

109
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
*I try again, but to little avail.*

110
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:28,000
Koichi: "Oh, spare me the excuses. You're starting to piss me off."

111
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Koichi: "Let's go, guys."

112
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Daigo: "Sure. Anything to get away from these two lovebirds."

113
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Kosuke: "Peh."

114
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:43,000
*Kosuke spits on the ground again before departing; skulking along in his beaten up winter coat behind Koichi and Daigo.*

115
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:46,000
*I watch them head off down the street, then sigh.*

116
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:49,000
*It's not yet 08:00, and I already feel exhausted.*

117
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:59,000
*I'm tired of being at odds with my housemates thanks to Hiyori. I used to get along with Koichi pretty well, until Hiyori began to cling to me like this.*

118
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:06,000
*I don't think she intended to drive a wedge between me and the guys, but that's how it ended up.*

119
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:11,000
*Maybe I'd feel less bitter about this if we were actually dating, but we're not.*

120
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:18,000
*It's all a genuine misunderstanding, but how can I tell my housemates that? They refuse to listen to me.*

121
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:26,000
*Hell, if I was in their shoes, I wouldn't listen to me, either. Hiyori's closeness does look awfully suspicious.*

122
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:36,000
*If only they understood that Hiyori has a few screws loose. That might salvage some goodwill from the wreckage of our capsized friendships...*

123
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,000
*But, then again, maybe not.*

124
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,000
*I shouldn't hold out any hope.*

125
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Hiyori: "Haru...?"

126
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:45,000
*Hiyori peers at me, her arm still looped through mine.*

127
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Hiyori: "Are you alright? You've gone very quiet."

128
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Hiyori: "You're not cold, are you?"

129
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Haru: "No, I'm fine. I'm just thinking."

130
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Hiyori: "About?"

131
00:11:54,000 --> 00:12:04,000
*I consider scolding Hiyori, then think better of it. She never listens to me. I doubt it'd do much good - and, in any case, I don't want to upset her.*

132
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
*I'd like to think of myself as a gentleman.*

133
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Haru: "Oh, it's nothing, really."

134
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:14,000
*I force a smile, then try to shrug Hiyori's grasping arm off mine.*

135
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Haru: "Would you mind letting go? It'll be hard to walk to university with you clinging like that."

136
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Haru: "I don't want to be late."

137
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:26,000
Hiyori: "Oh, right. You have a point, ehehe~"

138
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:35,000
Hiyori: "Sorry, sorry. When I see you, I just can't help myself. The embarrassed reactions of you humans are simply too charming!"

139
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Haru: "You're a human too, you know..."

140
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:42,000
*I mumble under my breath, but Hiyori doesn't seem to hear me.*

141
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:48,000
*She's good at conveniently blotting out remarks that conflict with her warped world view.*

142
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:53,000
*At least she lets go of me, at long last, which is something of a mercy.*

143
00:12:53,000 --> 00:13:03,000
*I do wish she'd relinquished her grip on me earlier, though. It would've saved me a lot of scrutinizing glares from my once-was trio of friends.*

144
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Haru: "Shall we head over to the campus, then?"

145
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,000
Hiyori: "Yes, let's!"

146
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:12,000
*Hiyori beams at me, her choppy brown hair shifting about her face.*

147
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:16,000
Hiyori: "Let's go together! We have a lot to discuss!"

148
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Hiyori: "We still need to plan out the finer details of tonight's hotpot party!"

149
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Haru: "Oh yeah... I'd almost forgotten about that."

150
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Hiyori: "It's good that you have me to remind you about these things then, isn't it?"

151
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Hiyori: "I swear, you humans would forget your heads if they weren't screwed onto your necks!"

152
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Hiyori: "How your race became the dominant force upon this planet, I shall never know. It really is a mystery!"

153
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Haru: "It isn't, really. Darwin did a lot of good work demystifying all that. Haven't you heard of "natural selection"?"

154
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:56,000
Hiyori: "Oh, really? I'm not good with complicated stuff like that, ehehe..."

155
00:13:56,000 --> 00:14:00,000
*Hiyori falls into step with me as we walk over to the campus.*

156
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:10,000
*The university's about half an hour away. We could take the bus or the train, but I prefer walking. I like to get a bit of exercise in every day.*

157
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:16,000
*I don't want to become a total slob, beholden to the convenience of public transport.*

158
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Hiyori: "So, about the hotpot party..."

159
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:24,000
*Hiyori says, once we've exhausted the subject of natural selection.*

160
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Hiyori: "I think we'll have it in the astronomy clubroom, after we're done stargazing on the roof."

161
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Hiyori: "I'll start cooking pretty late... Maybe around 21:00?"

162
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Hiyori: "How does that sound. Do you think you can hold out until then?"

163
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Haru: "That should be fine, yeah."

164
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:46,000
*I offer Hiyori a small smile, touched by her thoughtfulness.*

165
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:52,000
*That's one thing I can't fault her for. She's a considerate person... in some regards.*

166
00:14:52,000 --> 00:15:00,000
Haru: "I'll eat a big lunch. That should tide me over. Plus, your cooking's delicious. It's always worth waiting for."

167
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:02,000
*I'm not just saying that, either.*

168
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:14,000
*Hiyori's cooking is one of the pluses of being a member of the astronomy club. Though we're the astronomy club on paper, Hiyori treats the clubroom more like a restaurant.*

169
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:21,000
*Hiyori made chilled noodles in the summer, and now it's winter she's been preparing all kinds of warm dishes.*

170
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:37,000
*There's a brazier in the clubroom for grilling meat and stirring soups, and she even has a mini fridge to store ingredients. The fridge is perpetually full of veggies, plus the huge plastic cartons of barley tea Hiyori likes so much.*

171
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:42,000
*For all I grouse about Hiyori, she sure knows how to make the clubroom cozy.*

172
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Hiyori: "You charmer, you."

173
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:48,000
*Hiyori giggles, then nudges me in the side with her elbow.*

174
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Hiyori: "You know exactly what to say to girls to win them over..."

175
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Hiyori: "Not that I'm complaining."

176
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Hiyori: "Your tactics are even effective on me, though I am no ordinary girl!"

177
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Haru: "Yeah, yeah..."

178
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,000
*It always comes back to this with Hiyori.*

179
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:08,000
*Whenever I start thinking I might enjoy her company, she has to ruin the moment.*

180
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:18,000
*Sometimes I wonder why Hiyori is so desperate to stand out. While it's common to want to be special, people generally shed this desire when they get older.*

181
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:21,000
*Could it be a holdover from Hiyori's childhood?*

182
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:28,000
*Maybe her parents were neglectful? That might explain Hiyori's insatiable desire for attention...*

183
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
*Not that I can say for certain.*

184
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:37,000
*I don't know much about Hiyori's family. She's a chatterbox, but she hardly ever speaks about them.*

185
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Hiyori: "So, do you have any requests for tonight's hotpot? Is there anything in particular you want?"

186
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:48,000
Haru: "Not really - though I do like enoki mushrooms."

187
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Hiyori: "Well, yeah. Those are practically a given! Who doesn't put those in hotpot?"

188
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:57,000
Haru: "That's a good point. Then, uh..."

189
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:01,000
*I weigh up my options, all while running a hand through my hair.*

190
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Haru: "What about rice cake? I'm pretty fond of that."

191
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Hiyori: "Sure thing! I can pick some up from the supermarket, alongside the rest of the ingredients!"

192
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Hiyori: "And what about the broth? Do you have any special requests?"

193
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:21,000
Haru: "Anything's fine, so long as it's not too spicy."

194
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:28,000
Hiyori: "Now, that is a pity. You know how much I love spice - especially when it gets in your nose!"

195
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:33,000
Hiyori: "It feels good when you're eating hot food and you start to sneeze..."

196
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:37,000
Hiyori: "But I guess most humans don't like that, ehehe~"

197
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Haru: "No, we most certainly do not. You're so weird, Hiyori."

198
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Hiyori: "That should go without saying! I am an alien, after all!"

199
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:50,000
*Yeah, I know. She's told me about it enough times - not that I believe her.*

200
00:17:50,000 --> 00:18:01,000
*Her family name is Akasaka, for goodness' sake. That's about as basic as you can get. She's not that far removed from the Tanakas or the Suzukis of this world.*

201
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:04,000
*How many families called Akasaka dwell in space?*

202
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,000
*Not many, I'd be willing to bet.*

203
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:19,000
*If her family name was something like... oh, I don't know, "Cloudwalker", I might be more willing to take her wild claims about her alien lineage more seriously, but she's way too normal.*

204
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:24,000
*Everything about Hiyori is normal, really, save for these delusions of hers.*

205
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:36,000
*Sometimes, I wish Hiyori wasn't such a good cook. Then, I might have had the good sense to quit the astronomy club months ago, when she started spouting all this crazy nonsense.*

206
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:39,000
*I think it's too late for that now, though.*

207
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:44,000
*I decided to stick with Hiyori, and now I'm in it for the long haul.*

208
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:50,000
*At least her cooking's a good consolation prize, even if her waffle about aliens unnerves me.*

209
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Hiyori: "Hey, Haru."

210
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:58,000
*Hiyori's footsteps come to a halt. She peers at me, linking her arm through mine once more, and pouts.*

211
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:01,000
Hiyori: "Why aren't you saying anything?"

212
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Haru: "I don't have anything to say."

213
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:09,000
Hiyori: "But I just told you I was an alien! Doesn't that warrant some kind of reaction?"

214
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Haru: "You tell me you're an alien every day. I've gotten used to it."

215
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:17,000
Hiyori: "How can you get used to it?!"

216
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,000
*Hiyori pouts.*

217
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Hiyori: "It should be a revelation - particularly for a guy like you, who loves space! Doesn't it excite you?!"

218
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,000
Haru: "It's lost its luster."

219
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Hiyori: "Haru! I don't think you're treating this with the gravitas it deserves!"

220
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:43,000
Hiyori: "In fact, sometimes I think you don't believe me at all. Maybe you think I'm teasing you, or lying, but I'm not. I'm being honest! Everything I say is true!"

221
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Haru: "I believe that you believe everything you're saying is true, but as for me..."

222
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Hiyori: "You have your doubts?"

223
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,000
Haru: "A few, yeah. I mean..."

224
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,000
*I clear my throat.*

225
00:19:54,000 --> 00:20:01,000
*I don't want to be mean to Hiyori - not after she's been so kind to me - but I don't want to indulge her.*

226
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Haru: "You don't look anything like an alien. You seem like a regular human girl to me, in every regard."

227
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Hiyori: "That is what you think, but how can you say that for certain? You've never seen my whole body."

228
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:21,000
Hiyori: "If you knew what I looked like beneath my clothes, you might just reconsider."

229
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Haru: "Right. Er..."

230
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,000
*I frown.*

231
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:26,000
Haru: "I-Is that... supposed to be a pick-up line?"

232
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Hiyori: "Is that how you're interpreting it?"

233
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,000
*Hiyori smiles vaguely.*

234
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Hiyori: "Maybe it is. I don't think I'd mind if you saw me naked. I don't trust other humans, but you're special to me."

235
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Hiyori: "Am I not special to you, too?"

236
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:45,000
*Hiyori peers at me, her expression winsome.*

237
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,000
Hiyori: "We are friends, aren't we?"

238
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:53,000
Haru: "We are, sure, but it's because we're friends there are some things we shouldn't do!"

239
00:20:53,000 --> 00:21:01,000
*Such as getting naked in front of one another. That far surpasses the boundaries of mere "friendship" - in my eyes, at least.*

240
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:07,000
Haru: "Now, we've really gotta hurry, or we'll be late for class. I'm going to run."

241
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:09,000
Hiyori: "What? Hey, Haru!"

242
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:16,000
*Hiyori calls after me as I take off, the soles of my sneakers slapping against the dull, gray sidewalk.*

243
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:20,000
*I can't see Hiyori's face anymore, but I bet she's pouting.*

244
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:28,000
*Oh well. If she really is an alien, she can always summon her spaceship or something - not that this'll ever happen.*

245
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:33,000
*There's no way Hiyori's an alien, and I've no interest in humoring her.*

246
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,000
*It is, quite frankly, impossible.*

247
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:42,000
*I eventually arrive on campus, no thanks to Hiyori, and head over to my first lecture of the day.*

248
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:48,000
*I take a seat in the middle of the auditorium, and take notes while my professor talks.*

249
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:57,000
*I'm pretty passionate about my education, even this far into my course, which is more than can be said for some of my classmates.*

250
00:21:57,000 --> 00:22:05,000
*A few of my fellow students are slumped in seats at the very back of the room, trying to catch a covert forty winks.*

251
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:12,000
*I wonder if they stayed up late last night, partying. That's not an uncommon occurrence, even during weekdays.*

252
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:17,000
*I guess it is Friday today. My peers just couldn't wait for the weekend.*

253
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:29,000
*I don't really go to parties myself, unlike the others. Koichi used to invite me out, when I first moved into our apartment, but Hiyori's presence put paid to that pretty sharpish.*

254
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:37,000
*Hiyori might be one of the only friends I have, and I'm not entirely sure if she's my "friend", or somebody I simply endure.*

255
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:39,000
*I definitely don't hate her, but...*

256
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:40,000
*Hmm.*

257
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:41,000
*It's complicated.*

258
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:50,000
*Our relationship isn't nearly as complicated as physics, however. I have to focus, so I don't lose track of what the professor's saying.*

259
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:58,000
*I'm kept busy in lectures and seminars for the lion's share of the day. Fridays are particularly hectic for me.*

260
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:04,000
*It's a little after 18:00 when I finish with my final class, and the sky is already dark.*

261
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:11,000
*Since it's January, the sun sets pretty early. The campus is usually pitch black at half five or so.*

262
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:19,000
*I feel tired, thanks to all that frantic note-taking, and it's on weary limbs I haul myself off to the astronomy clubroom.*

263
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:26,000
*The astronomy clubroom is located in an out-of-the-way spot on the campus, a bit behind the library.*

264
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:38,000
*This is the oldest block of the university, and it's in dire need for refurbishment. The floors are wooden, and they creak when stepped on, like something from a horror movie.*

265
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:44,000
*The windows, meanwhile, are dirty from years of neglect, and all the doors creak.*

266
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:50,000
*This building is so woefully dated, I think it really might be a relic from the Taisho Era.*

267
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:54,000
*It has a pretty spooky vibe, particularly late at night.*

268
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:58,000
*I wouldn't be surprised if it were haunted by a ghost or two...*

269
00:23:58,000 --> 00:24:04,000
*Not that I believe in ghosts, of course. They're even less scientific than aliens.*

270
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:13,000
*There is, at least, a possibility that aliens might exist, though none have been recorded (sorry, Hiyori, but you don't count).*

271
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:18,000
*There is no hard evidence, however, that suggests ghosts might be real.*

272
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:24,000
*All fortune tellers are crooks, no matter what they say, and séances are a bunch of baloney.*

273
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:26,000
*I know that logically, and yet...*

274
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:27,000
*Creeeeeeak.*

275
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:32,000
*The floor creaks ominously beneath me, which sends a shiver down my spine.*

276
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:35,000
*This building really does give me the creeps.*

277
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:47,000
*It's so old, only a few rooms are used. The tiny clubs with hardly any members get shunted here, like the karuta club, which commands the ground floor, and the occult club.*

278
00:24:47,000 --> 00:25:05,000
*I don't really interact with members from either club. The members of the karuta club will all be smacking cards around, dressed in traditional Japanese attire (they really go all-out), and the last I heard of the occult club, they're busy trying to summon a demon.*

279
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:12,000
*I don't think their attempts are going too well, but I have no words of commiseration to offer them.*

280
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:18,000
*This place is eerie enough without it becoming a meet-up place for the denizens of hell.*

281
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:30,000
*Eventually, I make it to the third floor, where the astronomy clubroom's located. I open the door, which parts with a rattle like a dying man's last breath, and let myself inside.*

282
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:31,000
Hiyori: "Hey, Haru!"

283
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:34,000
*Hiyori greets me, smiling cheerfully.*

284
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:42,000
*Right now, she's kneeling by the fridge, which she's stuffing with packs of meat from a couple of carrier bags at her feet.*

285
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:46,000
*She swivels her head to look at me, though, still crouched.*

286
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:50,000
Hiyori: "It's so good to see you! Come in and have a seat!"

287
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:54,000
Haru: "You don't need to tell me that. I was planning on it."

288
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:59,000
*I close the door behind me, then deposit my bag down on the ground.*

289
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:00,000
Haru: "Geez..."

290
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:08,000
*I sink onto the well-worn couch with a sigh; not even bothering to remove my coat. That sounds too much like hard work.*

291
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:09,000
Haru: "I'm beat."

292
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:11,000
Hiyori: "Did you have a busy day?"

293
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:17,000
Haru: "Yeah, it was pretty intense. My hands are aching from taking so many notes."

294
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:25,000
Hiyori: "You could always use a laptop, you know. That might make things easier. A pencil and paper is so old school!"

295
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,000
Haru: "I guess..."

296
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:30,000
*I lean back on the couch and look up at the ceiling, frowning.*

297
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:36,000
*It's rare for Hiyori to come out with anything so sensible, but even she has her moments.*

298
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:44,000
Haru: "I prefer using a pen and paper, though. It feels easier to take in information, if I have to write out each character."

299
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:49,000
Haru: "Plus, it's what I'm used to. We didn't use laptops at my school very much."

300
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:53,000
Hiyori: "You went to a small school in the countryside, right?"

301
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Haru: "Uh-huh. It was really tiny. There were maybe eighty kids there, if there."

302
00:26:58,000 --> 00:26:59,000
Hiyori: "Wow."

303
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:00,000
*Hiyori whistles.*

304
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:05,000
Hiyori: "That is small. Coming here must have been a culture shock."

305
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:12,000
Haru: "It was, I guess... Not that I was utterly unfamiliar with the city. I wasn't a total bumpkin."

306
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:15,000
Haru: "I guess old habits die hard, though."

307
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:24,000
Haru: "I still don't feel comfy typing... which might be a problem, come to think of it, given I want to work on satellites when I graduate."

308
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:29,000
*I laugh weakly, but in my sleepy state, my laugh soon transmutes to a yawn.*

309
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:32,000
*When I blink, I can feel tears beading in my eyes.*

310
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:33,000
Hiyori: "My, my!"

311
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:40,000
*Hiyori shuts the fridge, then stands. She surveys me with a sweet smile, her head tilted, and says...*

312
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:45,000
Hiyori: "You really must be tired. Perhaps you should have a quick nap."

313
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:50,000
Haru: "Is that alright? I don't want to ruin our plans for tonight."

314
00:27:50,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Hiyori: "Oh, don't worry about it. It's fine! I can wake you up in an hour, and we can go stargazing then. The stars aren't going to go anywhere!"

315
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:07,000
Hiyori: "In fact, I think it's better if we wait. It's a bit too cloudy to break the telescope out now."

316
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:09,000
Haru: "Right... That sounds good..."

317
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:13,000
*I yawn again, but I stifle it with the palm of my right hand.*

318
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:22,000
*There's a red welt on the inside of my index finger, I note. That must be from gripping my pencil too tight. I get calluses pretty often.*

319
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:24,000
*Maybe I have sensitive skin?*

320
00:28:24,000 --> 00:28:33,000
*I wonder if this is a sign that I should start using my laptop during lectures after all. It seems a waste to have one and not use it.*

321
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:38,000
*It cost quite a lot of money, and my family isn't the wealthiest...*

322
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:39,000
Haru: "Aaah..."

323
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:40,000
*I yawn again.*

324
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:49,000
*The couch in the astronomy room is pretty soft, despite it being so old, and its comforting embrace is lulling me into the world of dreams.*

325
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:53,000
*My eyelids fall shut, and my breath soon begins to even out.*

326
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:56,000
Haru: "I think I'll take you up on that nap."

327
00:28:56,000 --> 00:29:01,000
Haru: "Wake me when you want to go to the roof, alright? I don't wanna miss out."

328
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:07,000
Hiyori: "I know. You're even crazier about the stars than I am, and that's where I came from."

329
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:08,000
*Hiyori giggles.*

330
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:13,000
Hiyori: "Leave everything in my capable hands. I'll look after you, Haru."

331
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:15,000
Hiyori: "For now, you should rest."

332
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:18,000
Haru: "Thanks. That sounds pretty good."

333
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:19,000
Haru: "Aaah."

334
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:25,000
*It's with this yawn, deeper than the last, that my conscience finally begins to fade.*

335
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:29,000
*Darkness consumes me, and my thoughts all slide into the abyss.*

336
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:30,000
*...*

337
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:31,000
*...*

338
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:32,000
*...*

339
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:36,000
Hiyori: "Hey, Haru. Wakey-wakey. You've had a full hour."

340
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:38,000
Haru: "Zzzz, mm... Huh?"

341
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:45,000
*I'm stirred from my torpor by a hand upon my shoulder, and a gentle exhalation of air against my cheek.*

342
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:46,000
*I shiver.*

343
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:49,000
*Slowly, I crack one eye open, then the other.*

344
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Hiyori: "Hey there, Haru."

345
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:57,000
*Hiyori greets me with a smile, her expression soft and gentle like a watercolor painting.*

346
00:29:57,000 --> 00:30:06,000
*She's kneeling in front of the couch, her face only inches away from mine. Her hands are resting on her knees; her head tilted to one side.*

347
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:10,000
*We're so close, our lips would brush if I were to lean in...*

348
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:12,000
*But, of course, I don't do that.*

349
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:20,000
*I don't know how, precisely, I feel about Hiyori, but I don't think I want to rush into any kind of relationship with her.*

350
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:23,000
*That sounds like more trouble than it's worth.*

351
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:35,000
*Still, it's not a bad way to be woken up. Being roused by my alarm clock during the cold wintry mornings is certainly less pleasant than being shaken into alertness by a smiling Hiyori.*

352
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:37,000
Haru: "Hey there yourself."

353
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:47,000
*I return Hiyori's greeting with one of my own, then sit up. My limbs feel a little stiff after napping for so long, and I still feel a touch fatigued.*

354
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:53,000
*I yawn, one hand pressed to my mouth. My eyes squeeze shut, tears beading on my lashes.*

355
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:56,000
*Why have I been feeling so sleepy lately?*

356
00:30:56,000 --> 00:31:02,000
*It must be the season. Winter always tires me out. It's so chilly, and it gets dark so early...*

357
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:05,000
*Not that the latter point bothers me too much.*

358
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:12,000
*Staring at the sun only hurts your eyes, but looking up at the moon can be a soothing, therapeutic experience.*

359
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:15,000
*I've always liked staring at the stars.*

360
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:16,000
*Speaking of which...*

361
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:19,000
Haru: "Are you ready to head up to the roof?"

362
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Hiyori: "I'm ready when you are!"

363
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:32,000
*Hiyori retrieves her own foldable telescope, which is a more powerful (and more expensive) model than mine, and tucks it under her arm. Then, she rises to her feet.*

364
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:38,000
Hiyori: "Shall we head on up? The clouds have cleared up a bunch since you started snoozing."

365
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:41,000
Hiyori: "It's a great night for stargazing!"

366
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Haru: "Great. I'm glad to hear that."

367
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:46,000
*I yawn again, then get to my own feet.*

368
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:48,000
Haru: "Let's go and take a look."

369
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:50,000
Hiyori: "Yessir! Roger that!"

370
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Haru: "Now, why are you calling me sir? You're the club leader, not me - and you're a year older than I am."

371
00:31:57,000 --> 00:32:02,000
Haru: "If anything, I should be the one bowing and scraping to you."

372
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:05,000
Hiyori: "I guess that is true, ehehe..."

373
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:12,000
Hiyori: "I wouldn't feel right bossing you around, though. I value you too much to treat you like that..."

374
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:19,000
Hiyori: "And, besides, you are the only member left in this club, other than myself. I can't scare you away!"

375
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:25,000
Hiyori: "I'm relying on you to stick by my side, even if everybody else has left me!"

376
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:28,000
Haru: "That sounds kind of needy, Hiyori."

377
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:32,000
Hiyori: "I am needy! I'm not ashamed of admitting it! I need you!"

378
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:34,000
Haru: "Well, uh... Gee..."

379
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:36,000
*I glance away, my face turning red.*

380
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:47,000
*I'm well aware that I'm indispensable to Hiyori, given my status as her sole fellow club member, but hearing it spelled out like that is kind of embarrassing.*

381
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:53,000
*Hiyori sounds so grateful, I wouldn't be surprised if she started groveling at my feet...*

382
00:32:53,000 --> 00:33:00,000
*Not that she could right now, given the telescope wedged beneath her arm. I doubt she'd want to drop it.*

383
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:03,000
*It's a very delicate piece of machinery.*

384
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:14,000
*...I should change the subject, for both the sake of my stammering heart, and Hiyori's telescope, which is just as indispensable to the astronomy club as I am.*

385
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:18,000
*Its destruction would put a bit of a damper on the night.*

386
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Haru: "I'm happy to hear that, I guess...?"

387
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:28,000
Haru: "Right now, however, we shouldn't be worrying about who owes who what. Let's just look at the stars."

388
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:30,000
Hiyori: "Alrighty then."

389
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:31,000
*Hiyori giggles.*

390
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:38,000
Hiyori: "Let's get this show on the road... Or, in this case, the roof! The last one there's a rotten egg!"

391
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:40,000
*Half an hour later...*

392
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Hiyori: "Wow! The stars all look so clear tonight! It almost feels like we aren't even in Tokyo!"

393
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:52,000
Hiyori: "We could be out in the countryside, away from all the lights and the cars..."

394
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:54,000
Hiyori: "It's incredible!"

395
00:33:54,000 --> 00:34:03,000
*Hiyori stares into the vast expanse of space which hangs above us, her right eye trained through the eyepiece of her telescope.*

396
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:11,000
*The telescope is set up by the edge of the roof; its optical tube tilted back and its thick lens directed at the sky.*

397
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:21,000
*Hiyori has been hogging the telescope ever since we got onto the roof, but I can't really fault her for it. The telescope does belong to her.*

398
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:24,000
*I'm fine with waiting for my turn...*

399
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:30,000
Hiyori: "Venus looks so close tonight! It almost feels like I could reach out and touch it!"

400
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:34,000
Hiyori: "I wonder if that's an omen of good fortune, ehehe."

401
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:39,000
*...Though Hiyori's cheery exclamations are making me itch with curiosity.*

402
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:45,000
*I want to take a good look at Venus, too - not that I haven't dozens of times in the past.*

403
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:58,000
*Seiji used to point all the planets and the constellations out to me during our walks. It's thanks to his tutelage that I've become so good at identifying the facets of our solar system.*

404
00:34:58,000 --> 00:35:04,000
*I've pored over the planets more often than most, but I've yet to grow tired of it.*

405
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:10,000
*Space is an endless source of fascination to me, perhaps because space itself is infinite.*

406
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:18,000
*There's only so much you can see of it, even with a telescope, but new discoveries are being made by scientists all the time.*

407
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:23,000
*I'd kill to get my hands on one of the heavy-duty telescopes they use in JAXA...*

408
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:30,000
*Well, maybe not quite (I don't like the sight of blood), but there's not much I wouldn't be prepared to do.*

409
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:33,000
*I guess you could say I'm obsessed with the stars.*

410
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:35,000
Hiyori: "Aaaah... This is so cool~"

411
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:39,000
*On this point, at least, Hiyori and I are in complete agreement.*

412
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:45,000
*I don't think we have all that much in common, but our shared love of space binds us together.*

413
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:52,000
*I could never bring myself to quit the astronomy club, no matter how touchy-feely Hiyori may be.*

414
00:35:52,000 --> 00:36:00,000
*These quiet moments spent together, observing space from the roof of the university, are all incredibly precious to me.*

415
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:01,000
Haru: "Brrr."

416
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:03,000
*...It is pretty chilly, though.*

417
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:10,000
*I jam my hands deep into my pockets, trying to fend off the worst of the cold, and tip my head back.*

418
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:20,000
*The moon greets my wandering eyes, round and white like an egg. I can't see its ridges too well, but I bet I could with the aid of Hiyori's telescope.*

419
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:24,000
*The moon is easy to spot, but no less fascinating for it.*

420
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:31,000
*It's the Earth's only natural satellite, and it's the fifth largest satellite in the solar system.*

421
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:36,000
*Other planets have more moons. Jupiter, for example, has seventy-nine.*

422
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:49,000
*Jupiter's largest moons are Io, Europa, Ganymede, and Callisto. They're not observable with the naked eye, but you can see them with binoculars, if the weather is right and you know where to look.*

423
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:54,000
*What other moons are there in the solar system, beyond Earth's orbit?*

424
00:36:54,000 --> 00:37:05,000
*Mercury and Venus aren't known to have any natural satellites, though there have been reports about a moon being spotted circling Venus since the 17th century.*

425
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:09,000
*Mars has two moons, Uranus twenty-seven, and Saturn...*

426
00:37:09,000 --> 00:37:11,000
*How many does it have?*

427
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:16,000
*I can't remember off the top of my head, though I know I did know this once.*

428
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:25,000
*I think it has more known moons than Jupiter, despite being the smaller of the two planets. Does it have eighty? Eighty-one...?*

429
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:28,000
*What are their names? I can't remember.*

430
00:37:28,000 --> 00:37:33,000
*Most moons are named after gods and goddesses; figures from antiquity.*

431
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:41,000
*I'm not too interested in Greek and Roman myth, but studying space got me into reading up on these old legends, too.*

432
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:43,000
*It's all pretty interesting...*

433
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:44,000
Haru: "Achoo!"

434
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:48,000
*But not even my musing can fully distract from how cold I am.*

435
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:56,000
*As much as I love the planets and the moons that circle them, I'll be glad to get back inside to sample Hiyori's hotpot.*

436
00:37:56,000 --> 00:37:58,000
*My poor fingers feel frozen.*

437
00:37:58,000 --> 00:37:59,000
Haru: "Hey, Hiyori."

438
00:37:59,000 --> 00:38:05,000
*I call out to the leader of the astronomy club, who's still parked in front of the telescope.*

439
00:38:05,000 --> 00:38:09,000
Haru: "Have you had your fill? I want to take a look now."

440
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:11,000
Hiyori: "Oh, I'm sorry about that."

441
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:17,000
*Hiyori glances at me from over her shoulder, then pokes out her tongue in apology.*

442
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:21,000
Hiyori: "I was so caught up, I forgot about you, ehehe~"

443
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:28,000
Hiyori: "Some senior I am, huh? I ought to look out for you more, Haru! You are my cute junior, after all!"

444
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:31,000
Haru: "I don't know if I'm all that "cute"..."

445
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:32,000
*My brow furrows.*

446
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:35,000
Haru: "But I am freezing my butt off."

447
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:38,000
Hiyori: "I bet your butt is awfully cute, too!"

448
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:42,000
Haru: "How would you know that? You've never seen it."

449
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:45,000
Hiyori: "Maybe not, but I can always imagine!"

450
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:49,000
Haru: "Please, don't imagine my butt. That's sexual harassment."

451
00:38:49,000 --> 00:38:51,000
Hiyori: "Oh, really? My apologies!"

452
00:38:51,000 --> 00:38:59,000
*Hiyori titters, then steps back from the telescope. She gestures towards it, dropping me a bow as she does so, like a butler.*

453
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:03,000
Hiyori: "It's all yours. Please, feel free to take a look."

454
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Haru: "Why, thank you kindly for your generosity."

455
00:39:06,000 --> 00:39:11,000
*I bow my head, a cynical smile on my face, and take my place by the telescope.*

456
00:39:11,000 --> 00:39:14,000
*I adjust the lens, then peer up at the night sky.*

457
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:19,000
*I drink in Venus, which - as Hiyori said - is very clear tonight...*

458
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:27,000
*Or, at least, as clear as Venus can be, given its surface is perpetually shrouded in shifting clouds of sulfuric acid.*

459
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:36,000
*Venus's rocky surface is enveloped completely in these clouds, but I can see patches of dark and light speckled across its surface.*

460
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
*I shift the telescope to the right, drinking in the stars that twinkle in the firmament.*

461
00:39:42,000 --> 00:39:49,000
*I'm more invested in the planets and their satellites than the stars, but the stars are very pretty, too.*

462
00:39:49,000 --> 00:39:54,000
*I'm content to simply gaze upon them, lost in the majesty of space...*

463
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:55,000
Haru: "Hmm?"

464
00:39:55,000 --> 00:39:57,000
*But something stops me short.*

465
00:39:57,000 --> 00:39:58,000
*I do a double-take.*

466
00:39:58,000 --> 00:40:06,000
*There's something cleaving through the sky, leaving a white trail behind like a cloud of exhaust from an airplane.*

467
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:09,000
*What could it be? A comet? Maybe a shooting star?*

468
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:10,000
Haru: "Hey, Hiyori..."

469
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:15,000
*I tear my eye away from the telescope and look to her, my brow furrowed.*

470
00:40:15,000 --> 00:40:17,000
Haru: "Did you see that?"

471
00:40:17,000 --> 00:40:18,000
Hiyori: "See what?"

472
00:40:18,000 --> 00:40:22,000
Haru: "That band of white light, just there... No, there!"

473
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:28,000
*I point to the sky, my arm outstretched like that alien from the popular American movie.*

474
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:40,000
*I thought the flicker I detected from the telescope might have been a figment of my imagination - it passed by so quickly, after all - but I can see the light again, with the naked eye.*

475
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:47,000
*There really is a tail of white light canvassing the sky - and, what's more, it seems to be getting closer.*

476
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:48,000
*What could it be?*

477
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:49,000
Hiyori: "Oh, wow..."

478
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:57,000
*Hiyori stares at the light, enraptured. Her mouth falls open in a small "o" of surprise, her hands clutched at her front.*

479
00:40:57,000 --> 00:41:03,000
Hiyori: "I think this is the first time I've seen a shooting star so clearly. It's very pretty!"

480
00:41:03,000 --> 00:41:07,000
Haru: "It is pretty, yeah - but is it really a shooting star?"

481
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:09,000
Hiyori: "What else would it be?"

482
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:18,000
Haru: "I don't know. That's what I'm trying to figure out. I think it's moving a bit too quickly for a shooting star, and that trajectory..."

483
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:19,000
*My brow furrows.*

484
00:41:19,000 --> 00:41:21,000
*I hope I'm imagining things, but...*

485
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:26,000
Haru: "Is it just me, or does it seem like it's heading in our direction?"

486
00:41:26,000 --> 00:41:33,000
*I stare at the pinprick of light, which grows bigger and more intense with every passing second.*

487
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:45,000
*I wasn't sure of my hypothesis, at first, but now I have no doubts. This star - if it really is a star - really is plummeting towards us, at a speed I can't even begin to fathom.*

488
00:41:45,000 --> 00:41:48,000
*It gets closer and closer still, until...*

489
00:41:48,000 --> 00:41:50,000
Haru: "Hiyori, look out!"

490
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:51,000
Hiyori: "Eeeek!!!"

491
00:41:51,000 --> 00:42:02,000
*I push the transfixed Hiyori to the side, hoping to rescue her from the blast zone of the falling piece of space debris, and land on the university roof with a dull thud.*

492
00:42:02,000 --> 00:42:10,000
*Pain sears through my leg, short and sharp. The air forces its way from my lungs, and I gag on the crisp night air.*

493
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:19,000
*When I glance up, my vision hazy, I can see the object is still shuttling towards us, so white and bright it hurts my eyes to look at it.*

494
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:23,000
*It's pretty, but I've no doubts, now, that it's deadly, too.*

495
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:29,000
*I'll not be able to escape its blast zone - not on my injured leg - but maybe Hiyori can?*

496
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:38,000
*That seems like wishful thinking (on impact, this thing'll be sure to leave behind a massive crater), but I don't want to abandon hope.*

497
00:42:38,000 --> 00:42:41,000
Haru: "You have to run, Hiyori! Get out of here!"

498
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:44,000
Hiyori: "What? But, Haru, what about you?!"

499
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:48,000
Haru: "I-I'll be fine. You go on without me, please. Hiyori,  I-"

500
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:52,000
*I say... but I can't finish the rest of my sentence.*

501
00:42:52,000 --> 00:42:59,000
*I feel something collide with me, knocking what little air out of my lungs which still remained.*

502
00:42:59,000 --> 00:43:00,000
Haru:  "Guh!!!"

503
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
*I cough, choking on nothing, my head smacking against the roof with another thud.*

504
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:08,000
*Then, everything goes black.*

505
00:43:08,000 --> 00:43:09,000
*...*

506
00:43:09,000 --> 00:43:10,000
*...*

507
00:43:10,000 --> 00:43:11,000
*...*

508
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:14,000
Hiyori: "...ru? Are you alright, Haru...?!"

509
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:15,000
Haru: "Nn... What...?"

510
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:21,000
*I blink groggily, then finally - after what seems a small eternity - open my eyes.*

511
00:43:21,000 --> 00:43:28,000
*My head is throbbing something fierce, and Hiyori's panicky voice isn't doing much to assuage its aching.*

512
00:43:28,000 --> 00:43:32,000
*My limbs, meanwhile, feel very heavy; my legs in particular.*

513
00:43:32,000 --> 00:43:34,000
*What in the world happened?*

514
00:43:34,000 --> 00:43:40,000
*I remember I was standing on the rooftop, looking up at the night sky, and the next...*

515
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:47,000
Hiyori: "Oh, thank goodness you're alright! I was so worried about you! You were out cold for ages!"

516
00:43:47,000 --> 00:43:48,000
Haru: "Really...?"

517
00:43:48,000 --> 00:43:49,000
*I frown.*

518
00:43:49,000 --> 00:43:50,000
Haru: "Define "ages"."

519
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:58,000
Hiyori: "I can't rightly say, I was in such a state. I wasn't keeping a track of the time. It felt like a long while..."

520
00:43:58,000 --> 00:44:03,000
Hiyori: "But, now that I think about it, maybe it was only a few minutes?"

521
00:44:03,000 --> 00:44:07,000
Hiyori: "You were so still, though, you looked like a doll..."

522
00:44:07,000 --> 00:44:08,000
Hiyori: "Or a corpse."

523
00:44:08,000 --> 00:44:09,000
*Hiyori shudders.*

524
00:44:09,000 --> 00:44:15,000
Hiyori: "Still, you're awake now, and that's all that matters. How is your head? Does it hurt?"

525
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:21,000
Haru: "A bit, yeah. I feel pretty funny. I should be alright, though. Let me try to sit up..."

526
00:44:21,000 --> 00:44:23,000
*I make an attempt to sit, but...*

527
00:44:23,000 --> 00:44:24,000
Haru: "Huh?"

528
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:26,000
*It's to little avail.*

529
00:44:26,000 --> 00:44:27,000
*What's going on...?*

530
00:44:27,000 --> 00:44:34,000
*I feel alright, despite the dull throbbing in my skull, but my body refuses to obey me. Why can't I stand?*

531
00:44:34,000 --> 00:44:37,000
*I haven't lost the use of my legs, have I?*

532
00:44:37,000 --> 00:44:44,000
*They feel disconcertingly numb - but at least I can feel them. That has to count for something, right?*

533
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:48,000
*I can see well enough, and my vision isn't blurring.*

534
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:50,000
*As for my legs, however...*

535
00:44:50,000 --> 00:44:52,000
*I look up, my brow furrowed, and...*

536
00:44:52,000 --> 00:44:53,000
Haru: "Ah."

537
00:44:53,000 --> 00:45:02,000
*A single exclamation falls from my lips. It's only a single syllable, but it communicates my surprise better than any essay could.*

538
00:45:02,000 --> 00:45:05,000
*Now I see why my legs feel so strange.*

539
00:45:05,000 --> 00:45:09,000
*This whole situation, or so it seems, is strange in general.*

540
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:19,000
???: "Greetings earthling, whose name I believe is "Haru". It is a pleasure to meet you, though I fear it is not under the best circumstances."

541
00:45:19,000 --> 00:45:26,000
???: "I must apologize profusely for running into you! I only hope I have not caused you too many problems?"

542
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:32,000
*There's somebody sitting on top of me - and quite a distinctive "somebody" at that.*

543
00:45:32,000 --> 00:45:37,000
*A woman is perched on my lap, her plump thighs splayed, pinning me in place.*

544
00:45:37,000 --> 00:45:43,000
*Her skin looks smooth and her eyes large, which - when combined - makes her look youthful.*

545
00:45:43,000 --> 00:45:51,000
*If I had to guess her age, I'd put her in the same bracket as Hiyori and I; in her very late teens to very early twenties.*

546
00:45:51,000 --> 00:45:56,000
*Maybe she's twenty-one, twenty-two? It's hard to say with certainty.*

547
00:45:56,000 --> 00:46:06,000
*Her hair is long and pale green, like sea foam. It falls over her shoulders, fluttering in the cool breeze which bites through my coat and shirt.*

548
00:46:06,000 --> 00:46:19,000
*Though it's a cold night, this woman has foregone practical attire. She's wearing clothes the likes of which I've never seen before, outside of silly sci-fi flicks and Halloween costumes.*

549
00:46:19,000 --> 00:46:30,000
*I'm not even sure how to describe her get-up (my aching head and general disorientation isn't helping), but if put on the spot, I guess I'd say that she's...*

550
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:37,000
*Backlit by the moon as she is, with the stars twinkling beyond her, this woman looks almost ethereal...*

551
00:46:37,000 --> 00:46:39,000
*Or maybe extraterrestrial.*

552
00:46:39,000 --> 00:46:41,000
*What did she say to me just now?*

553
00:46:41,000 --> 00:46:51,000
*My mind isn't working properly (that fall really did a number on my head), and this woman's sudden, inexplicable appearance makes it chug slower still.*

554
00:46:51,000 --> 00:46:53,000
*Did she call me an "earthling"?*

555
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:55,000
*Then, would that make her...*

556
00:46:55,000 --> 00:46:56,000
Haru: "A-An alien?"

557
00:46:56,000 --> 00:47:02,000
???: "I suppose that is how I must seem, to you, though I have never considered myself as such."

558
00:47:02,000 --> 00:47:06,000
???: "To me, you are the alien; you and your friend..."

559
00:47:06,000 --> 00:47:11,000
???: "But, as I am on your planet now, I must oblige by your customs."

560
00:47:11,000 --> 00:47:22,000
???: "I am an outsider, so I will not take any offense at being called an "alien". You may call me that if you wish, if it will make things easier for you to understand!"

561
00:47:22,000 --> 00:47:25,000
Haru: "Wow, uh... H-How considerate of you..."

562
00:47:25,000 --> 00:47:29,000
???: "Do you really think so? That makes me very happy!"

563
00:47:29,000 --> 00:47:39,000
???: "This is the first time I have ever been to this planet of yours - which is very lovely, by the way - and I am not entirely sure how I ought to act."

564
00:47:39,000 --> 00:47:45,000
???: "I do not fully understand the customs of you earthlings, but I am willing to try!"

565
00:47:45,000 --> 00:47:50,000
???: "Please do not berate me too harshly if I cause offense, though!"

566
00:47:50,000 --> 00:47:53,000
Haru: "O-Oh, no. There's, uh, no offense taken..."

567
00:47:53,000 --> 00:48:01,000
*Honestly, I'm so stunned by this chain of events, I don't know what to say. My mouth must be working on autopilot.*

568
00:48:01,000 --> 00:48:04,000
*I'm sure this must be some kind of crazy dream...*

569
00:48:04,000 --> 00:48:10,000
*But, no, the alien girl on my lap feels too warm - not to mention too solid - for that.*

570
00:48:10,000 --> 00:48:12,000
*Speaking of the alien girl...*

571
00:48:12,000 --> 00:48:14,000
Haru: "So, uh... What's your name?"

572
00:48:14,000 --> 00:48:22,000
Ena: "I am Ena Satellia Ananke VII, Crown Princess of Corval, which is located in sector nine of the Ankh Galaxy..."

573
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:26,000
*Wow. That's a lot to remember, even for a space nerd like me.*

574
00:48:26,000 --> 00:48:30,000
*I've never even heard of the "Ankh Galaxy" before, or Corval.*

575
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:34,000
*It seems there's a lot about space I don't know about.*

576
00:48:34,000 --> 00:48:38,000
Ena: "...but you can just call me "Ena", if that is easier!"

577
00:48:38,000 --> 00:48:49,000
Ena: "I tired of the restrictions of my home planet, and of my duties as a princess, and so decided to go on a jaunt through the galaxies to find somewhere more..."

578
00:48:49,000 --> 00:48:52,000
Ena: "Hospitable, I suppose you could say."

579
00:48:52,000 --> 00:48:58,000
Ena: "I have heard good feelings about this humble planet of yours, so decided to come here!"

580
00:48:58,000 --> 00:49:04,000
Ena: "I might have been a bit too eager while initiating the landing sequence, however."

581
00:49:04,000 --> 00:49:13,000
Ena: "My poor ship broke apart in your planet's atmosphere, though my power suit was able to protect me from the worst of the impact."

582
00:49:13,000 --> 00:49:19,000
Ena: "That, and the very kind, considerate boy who offered himself as a shield to protect me!"

583
00:49:19,000 --> 00:49:22,000
Haru: "What? Oh, uh... Don't mention it."

584
00:49:22,000 --> 00:49:24,000
Ena: "But I must mention it!"

585
00:49:24,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Ena: "It was very good of you to catch me as I fell from the sky. Your thoughtfulness made my heart flutter - and so, hasty though this might sound, I believe I have come to a decision!"

586
00:49:36,000 --> 00:49:37,000
Haru: "What...?"

587
00:49:37,000 --> 00:49:44,000
Ena: "I am tired of being Corval's princess! I would rather stay here, on Earth, and become your bride!"

588
00:49:44,000 --> 00:49:48,000
Ena: "Does not that not sound like a wonderful idea?!"

589
00:49:48,000 --> 00:49:51,000
Haru: "It's certainly an idea, but..."

590
00:49:51,000 --> 00:49:58,000
*I agree with Ena, still operating on autopilot - until my last vestiges of common sense kick in.*

591
00:49:58,000 --> 00:50:06,000
*It's hard to think through the fog that's swirling about in my skull, but didn't she say something incredible just then?*

592
00:50:06,000 --> 00:50:07,000
Haru: "Wait..."

593
00:50:07,000 --> 00:50:09,000
*My brow furrows, and then...*

594
00:50:09,000 --> 00:50:13,000
Haru: "L-Like I'd agree to marry you! I've only just met you!"

595
00:50:13,000 --> 00:50:15,000
Haru: "This is insane!"

596
00:50:15,000 --> 00:50:18,000
Ena: "Huh? Does this mean you won't marry me?"

597
00:50:18,000 --> 00:50:25,000
Haru: "Sorry, but no. I'm too young to think about marriage - and, like I said on the roof, I hardly know you."

598
00:50:25,000 --> 00:50:33,000
Ena: "You do know me, though! You know that my name is Ena Satellia Ananke VII, and that I am the Princess of Corval!"

599
00:50:33,000 --> 00:50:37,000
Ena: "What more information could you possibly need?!"

600
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:40,000
Hiyori: "I don't mean to butt in, but..."

601
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:47,000
*Hiyori butts in - but, for once, I appreciate it. I'm having a hard time dealing with Ena on my own.*

602
00:50:47,000 --> 00:50:52,000
*She might be even clingier than Hiyori herself, which is saying something.*

603
00:50:52,000 --> 00:50:55,000
Hiyori: "You say you are an alien, yes...?"

604
00:50:55,000 --> 00:50:57,000
Ena: "Yes, that's right!"

605
00:50:57,000 --> 00:51:00,000
Hiyori: "And you come from another planet?"

606
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:01,000
Ena: "Indeed!"

607
00:51:01,000 --> 00:51:02,000
Hiyori: "Wow..."

608
00:51:02,000 --> 00:51:05,000
*Hiyori leans back on the couch, her eyes wide.*

609
00:51:05,000 --> 00:51:13,000
Hiyori: "That really is amazing. I always knew there were intelligent alien lifeforms out there! This really is incredible!"

610
00:51:13,000 --> 00:51:17,000
Hiyori: "I'm so glad to meet a fellow extraterrestrial!"

611
00:51:17,000 --> 00:51:20,000
Hiyori: "It's nice not being so alone, ehehe~"

612
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:21,000
Ena: "A fellow...?"

613
00:51:21,000 --> 00:51:23,000
*Ena tilts her head askance.*

614
00:51:23,000 --> 00:51:26,000
Ena: "Are you not an earthling yourself, Hiyori?"

615
00:51:26,000 --> 00:51:37,000
Hiyori: "I have reason to believe so, yes. Though I have parents on this planet, who have raised me since I was a child, I do not think they are related to me."

616
00:51:37,000 --> 00:51:44,000
Hiyori: "I have good reason to believe I was adopted, though my parents will not confirm my theories."

617
00:51:44,000 --> 00:51:50,000
Hiyori: "They always tell me not to be so fanciful, like I'm saying all this without proof!"

618
00:51:50,000 --> 00:51:52,000
Hiyori: "It's kind of tiring..."

619
00:51:52,000 --> 00:51:54,000
*Hiyori sighs, then shakes her head.*

620
00:51:54,000 --> 00:51:58,000
Hiyori: "But enough about me! We should be talking about you!"

621
00:51:58,000 --> 00:52:03,000
Hiyori: "I'm really happy to meet you! I hope we can become good friends!"

622
00:52:03,000 --> 00:52:14,000
Ena: "Me too! I would like some companions, now I have arrived upon this planet. I have never before left the Ankh Galaxy, but I do have some knowledge about Earth."

623
00:52:14,000 --> 00:52:22,000
Ena: "I have seen some of your shows, and read some of your books, so I have a smattering of knowledge about your ways."

624
00:52:22,000 --> 00:52:23,000
Haru: "Oh, really?"

625
00:52:23,000 --> 00:52:27,000
*Now, this is an interesting piece of news to chew on.*

626
00:52:27,000 --> 00:52:31,000
Haru: "How were you able to get your hands on all that stuff?"

627
00:52:31,000 --> 00:52:41,000
Ena: "I had it imported! Traders make frequent stops upon this planet, or so I have heard, to buy goods, which they resell in Corval for marked up prices."

628
00:52:41,000 --> 00:52:49,000
Ena: "Few people can afford earthling entertainment, which is highly-prized, but currency has never been an issue for me."

629
00:52:49,000 --> 00:52:53,000
Ena: "I am the daughter of the Ananke family, after all!"

630
00:52:53,000 --> 00:52:57,000
Haru: "Right... So, uh, is that how you learned Japanese?"

631
00:52:57,000 --> 00:53:02,000
Ena: "Yes, indeed! Your manga, as I believe you call it, taught me a good deal!"

632
00:53:02,000 --> 00:53:11,000
Ena: "I do so love reading manga - particularly the four panel ones, with funny jokes. They always lifted my spirits when I felt down!"

633
00:53:11,000 --> 00:53:21,000
Ena: "I have longed since my childhood to visit the planet which produced such amusing tales, so that I might better immerse myself in your culture!"

634
00:53:21,000 --> 00:53:25,000
Ena: "There is much I do not know, but I am willing to learn!"

635
00:53:25,000 --> 00:53:29,000
Ena: "I want to discover all Earth has to offer with you, darling!"

636
00:53:29,000 --> 00:53:36,000
*Ena's bright smile pierces my heart. She's so earnestly optimistic, I can't help but find her charming.*

637
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:39,000
*It doesn't hurt that she's so pretty, either.*

638
00:53:39,000 --> 00:53:52,000
*It's a relief that, despite being an alien, she's undoubtedly humanoid. She has the correct configuration of limbs (as far as I can see), only one head, and her teeth don't seem to be razor sharp.*

639
00:53:52,000 --> 00:54:05,000
*If she were a space octopus with squirming tentacles, I'd find it hard talking to her, no matter how well-meaning she is, but she looks so like a regular human it's pretty easy to talk to her.*

640
00:54:05,000 --> 00:54:09,000
*That outfit of hers really is something else, though.*

641
00:54:09,000 --> 00:54:19,000
*I find my eyes sliding to her chest continuously, no matter how I try to avert my eyes. It's almost as though her chest has its own gravitational field.*

642
00:54:19,000 --> 00:54:22,000
Haru: "It's, uh, good to meet you, Ena... Ahem..."

643
00:54:22,000 --> 00:54:26,000
*I clear my throat, in an attempt to regain my composure.*

644
00:54:26,000 --> 00:54:37,000
Haru: "But I'm not sure about your marriage proposal. We've not known one another long enough to consider it, and I'm too young to make such a life-altering decision."

645
00:54:37,000 --> 00:54:40,000
Haru: "We might have to put that on hold for now."

646
00:54:40,000 --> 00:54:41,000
Ena: "What, really?"

647
00:54:41,000 --> 00:54:42,000
*Ena pouts.*

648
00:54:42,000 --> 00:54:48,000
Ena: "But I was hoping we could be wed forthwith, to secure my citizenship upon this planet!"

649
00:54:48,000 --> 00:54:52,000
Ena: "I have absolutely no desire to return back home!"

650
00:54:52,000 --> 00:54:54,000
Hiyori: "Won't you miss your family?"

651
00:54:54,000 --> 00:55:03,000
Ena: "Somewhat, I suppose. My parents have been nothing but nice to me - but they have always put me under a good deal of pressure."

652
00:55:03,000 --> 00:55:11,000
Ena: "Whenever they speak to me, it is to warn me about my manners, or to coach me about my eventual ascension to the throne."

653
00:55:11,000 --> 00:55:15,000
Ena: "I have no desire to deal with that sort of stress."

654
00:55:15,000 --> 00:55:23,000
Ena: "I want to read more manga, and watch anime, and explore this country - and I wish to do all that with you, darling!"

655
00:55:23,000 --> 00:55:32,000
*Ena launches herself at me, but I pre-empted this, and am able to shuffle back on the couch before she can envelop me in her embrace.*

656
00:55:32,000 --> 00:55:39,000
*I've gotten pretty good at dodging exultant displays of affection, thanks to the months I've known Hiyori.*

657
00:55:39,000 --> 00:55:42,000
*I guess you could call it a talent of mine.*

658
00:55:42,000 --> 00:55:45,000
Haru: "I, uh, appreciate the gesture..."

659
00:55:45,000 --> 00:55:48,000
*I eye Ena with some trepidation, my arms folded.*

660
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:55,000
Haru: "But, like I said, this really is too sudden. I haven't even graduated from university yet!"

661
00:55:55,000 --> 00:55:56,000
Ena: "University...?"

662
00:55:56,000 --> 00:56:04,000
Haru: "Higher education. It comes after high school. Haven't you read about it, in all the manga you like so much?"

663
00:56:04,000 --> 00:56:13,000
Ena: "It is a new concept to me. The manga I read all revolved around cute girls, and they attended institutions known as "high schools"."

664
00:56:13,000 --> 00:56:18,000
Ena: "I was not aware human education persisted beyond such boundaries!"

665
00:56:18,000 --> 00:56:21,000
Haru: "I guess that's not too surprising..."

666
00:56:21,000 --> 00:56:30,000
*I don't read much manga myself, but from what I know, these kinds of things do tend to depict overly idyllic lives of high school students.*

667
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:41,000
*University, by contrast, is more stressful. You're already an adult by the time you get to university, and you've got to start worrying seriously about the future.*

668
00:56:41,000 --> 00:56:47,000
*The university experience is a bit harder to cute-ify than careless high school antics.*

669
00:56:47,000 --> 00:56:51,000
Haru: "This room here, that we're sitting in right now..."

670
00:56:51,000 --> 00:56:53,000
*I gesture with my arms.*

671
00:56:53,000 --> 00:56:57,000
Haru: "...is a clubroom in a wing of our university."

672
00:56:57,000 --> 00:57:02,000
Haru: "Hiyori and I are both students. She's one year older than I am."

673
00:57:02,000 --> 00:57:13,000
Haru: "I'm studying physics, with the hope of getting a good job once I graduate. I need to work hard, or all my efforts - and all my money - will go to waste."

674
00:57:13,000 --> 00:57:15,000
Haru: "University isn't cheap."

675
00:57:15,000 --> 00:57:20,000
Haru: "I really can't afford to get married now. It isn't very practical."

676
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:25,000
Ena: "Oh, I see. I suppose I understand. That is unfortunate, but..."

677
00:57:25,000 --> 00:57:26,000
*Ena's eyes light up.*

678
00:57:26,000 --> 00:57:34,000
Ena: "That simply means I will have to wait until you have graduated! Then, there will be nothing to stop our wedding!"

679
00:57:34,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Haru: "Yeah, about that..."

680
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:38,000
*I run a hand through my hair.*

681
00:57:38,000 --> 00:57:42,000
Haru: "How long do you think it'll take me to graduate, anyway?"

682
00:57:42,000 --> 00:57:51,000
Ena: "I do not know. I am not familiar with human customs such as "graduation" - and your days do not pass as they do in Corval."

683
00:57:51,000 --> 00:57:55,000
Ena: "It is hard for me to give a proper estimate, but... Hmm."

684
00:57:55,000 --> 00:57:59,000
Ena: "Would it, perchance, take... two of your Earthen weeks?"

685
00:57:59,000 --> 00:58:00,000
Haru: "Two weeks?"

686
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:01,000
*I shake my head.*

687
00:58:01,000 --> 00:58:05,000
*I think this girl might be laboring under a misapprehension here.*

688
00:58:05,000 --> 00:58:06,000
Haru: "Try two years."

689
00:58:06,000 --> 00:58:07,000
Ena: "Huh?!"

690
00:58:07,000 --> 00:58:08,000
*Ena's eyes widen.*

691
00:58:08,000 --> 00:58:10,000
Ena: "But that is a long time!"

692
00:58:10,000 --> 00:58:19,000
Haru: "It is, yeah. That's why you should probably give up on the idea. I doubt you'd want to hang around here for that long, waiting on me."

693
00:58:19,000 --> 00:58:26,000
Ena: "It is true, it is an inconvenient amount of time. I was hoping the process would be much swifter..."

694
00:58:26,000 --> 00:58:33,000
Ena: "But if you say I must wait two years before you will consider my proposal, then that is what I will do!"

695
00:58:33,000 --> 00:58:42,000
Ena: "I do not plan to return to Corval any time soon, you see. I would far rather be your wife than a princess! It sounds like fun!"

696
00:58:42,000 --> 00:58:49,000
*She did say that before, didn't she? She wants to marry me so she doesn't have to become a queen.*

697
00:58:49,000 --> 00:58:54,000
*I don't know if avoidance is the best reason for a couple to get married...*

698
00:58:54,000 --> 00:59:02,000
*But couples on this planet get married for spurious reasons all the time. "Love" isn't the only factor; not by a long shot.*

699
00:59:02,000 --> 00:59:09,000
*What Ena's suggesting isn't all that uncommon, actually, not that I'm planning to tell her that.*

700
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:14,000
*I don't want to give her any further ammunition to fuel her delusions.*

701
00:59:14,000 --> 00:59:16,000
*Does she actually like me, anyway?*

702
00:59:16,000 --> 00:59:22,000
*Her friendliness is awfully effusive, but perhaps that's just part of her culture...?*

703
00:59:22,000 --> 00:59:24,000
*I'm busy pondering this, when...*

704
00:59:24,000 --> 00:59:25,000
Ena: "Oh!"

705
00:59:25,000 --> 00:59:30,000
*Ena jumps, alarmed, as a low rumbling sound emits from her stomach.*

706
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:35,000
*Smiling bashfully, she rests one hand upon her abdomen, then says...*

707
00:59:35,000 --> 00:59:42,000
Ena: "My apologies for that most ungracious sound, ehehe. I apologize if I have caused any offense."

708
00:59:42,000 --> 00:59:45,000
Hiyori: "It's alright! You can't help being hungry!"

709
00:59:45,000 --> 00:59:50,000
Hiyori: "I imagine you haven't eaten a while, since you left the palace?"

710
00:59:50,000 --> 00:59:58,000
Ena: "That is, indeed, correct. I was so caught up in my attempts to flee my home planet, I did not think to eat beforehand."

711
00:59:58,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Ena: "Revi made me some snacks to eat during my flight - she is my maid - but they were not nearly enough to sustain me."

712
01:00:06,000 --> 01:00:11,000
Ena: "I have had a long journey across the cosmos, and I am rather peckish."

713
01:00:11,000 --> 01:00:19,000
Ena: "I was hoping to stop at a Moonbucks along the way, but I did not bring any space dollars with me, in my haste."

714
01:00:19,000 --> 01:00:20,000
Haru: "Moonbucks...?"

715
01:00:20,000 --> 01:00:22,000
Ena: "You do not know it?"

716
01:00:22,000 --> 01:00:27,000
Haru: "I know something like it. Does it, by any chance, sell coffee?"

717
01:00:27,000 --> 01:00:29,000
Ena: "Yes, indeed! How did you know?"

718
01:00:29,000 --> 01:00:31,000
Haru: "It was a lucky guess..."

719
01:00:31,000 --> 01:00:40,000
Ena: "I am partial to Moonbucks's black hole and stardust frappe with proton sauce and extra quasars, but alas! I could not afford one!"

720
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:43,000
Ena: "I fear I have missed my chance now..."

721
01:00:43,000 --> 01:00:44,000
Ena: "Sob, sob."

722
01:00:44,000 --> 01:00:51,000
Hiyori: "I don't know about "black hole frappes", but I can make you something warm and nourishing to eat!"

723
01:00:51,000 --> 01:00:54,000
Ena: "Can you really? Would that not be a burden?"

724
01:00:54,000 --> 01:01:01,000
Hiyori: "Not at all! Haru and I were planning to have hotpot tonight anyway, after we were finished stargazing."

725
01:01:01,000 --> 01:01:10,000
Hiyori: "You're more than welcome to join in! I bought plenty of ingredients! I don't think Haru and I would be able to finish it all anyway!"

726
01:01:10,000 --> 01:01:11,000
Ena: ""Hotpot"?"

727
01:01:11,000 --> 01:01:12,000
*Ena blinks.*

728
01:01:12,000 --> 01:01:14,000
Ena: "What is that, pray tell?"

729
01:01:14,000 --> 01:01:16,000
Haru: "Haven't you heard of it?"

730
01:01:16,000 --> 01:01:17,000
*Ena shakes her head.*

731
01:01:17,000 --> 01:01:25,000
Ena: "I presume, from the name, it is a meal served in a pot, at a high temperature, but other than that I am quite lost!"

732
01:01:25,000 --> 01:01:36,000
Haru: "Yeah, that's about right. You fill a bot with broth, which you warm up over a stove, and you throw a bunch of ingredients into it: mostly meat and veggies."

733
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:41,000
Haru: "Then, you wait for it to cook, and pick out whatever you want."

734
01:01:41,000 --> 01:01:47,000
Ena: "Would that not get violent, if everybody is trying to grab bits of food at the same time?"

735
01:01:47,000 --> 01:01:53,000
Ena: "I know, on this planet, people eat with sticks that seem useful for gouging."

736
01:01:53,000 --> 01:02:00,000
Ena: "Are you meant to battle for dominance, and stab your opponents in the eye with these sticks?"

737
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:07,000
Haru: "No, uh... You've got it totally wrong. You're not meant to fight over the hotpot. That'd be bad manners."

738
01:02:07,000 --> 01:02:18,000
Hiyori: "You don't need to worry about not getting enough food, Ena. There's more than enough to eat - and I'll make sure to set you aside some delicious meat!"

739
01:02:18,000 --> 01:02:22,000
Ena: "Oh, I see... Thank you for clarifying. I feel at ease now."

740
01:02:22,000 --> 01:02:28,000
Ena: "For a while, I was worried our leisurely meal would descend into chaos and anarchy, ehehe."

741
01:02:28,000 --> 01:02:35,000
*I guess Ena wouldn't be a fan of anarchism, given her home planet seems to be governed by a royal family.*

742
01:02:35,000 --> 01:02:37,000
*Isn't that kind of archaic?*

743
01:02:37,000 --> 01:02:44,000
*Does her family rule over the whole planet or just part of it? If it is the former, would they be dictators?*

744
01:02:44,000 --> 01:02:45,000
*Space dictators?*

745
01:02:45,000 --> 01:02:49,000
*I wonder if that plays a part in why Ena decided to leave.*

746
01:02:49,000 --> 01:02:53,000
Haru: "I'm surprised you've never heard of hotpot, though."

747
01:02:53,000 --> 01:02:55,000
*I muse aloud, arms crossed.*

748
01:02:55,000 --> 01:03:04,000
Haru: "It's a popular dish; especially in the winter. Families often eat it together, and groups of friends. It's a good way to bond."

749
01:03:04,000 --> 01:03:08,000
Haru: "Did you not come across it in any of the manga you read?"

750
01:03:08,000 --> 01:03:15,000
Ena: "No, I did not. I only had access to a small handful of series, even with my family's influence."

751
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:21,000
Ena: "There is still much I do not know - but I am aware of sushi, at the very least!"

752
01:03:21,000 --> 01:03:29,000
Hiyori: "Sushi, huh? Maybe we should have that together some time. We could order a huge platter and share it, ehehe~"

753
01:03:29,000 --> 01:03:33,000
Ena: "Ooh, that sounds good! I would very much like to try it!"

754
01:03:33,000 --> 01:03:41,000
Hiyori: "Maybe we can, in the future. For now, let us stick to the hotpot. I'll start preparing all the ingredients!"

755
01:03:41,000 --> 01:03:45,000
*Hiyori gets to her feet, then rolls up her sleeves.*

756
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:53,000
Hiyori: "We shouldn't need to do all that much prep work. Hotpot isn't too hard to make, and it tastes incredible."

757
01:03:53,000 --> 01:03:58,000
Hiyori: "I'm sure you'll love it, Ena. Just leave everything to me!"

758
01:03:58,000 --> 01:04:02,000
Ena: "So, is this the so-called "hotpot" you spoke of so highly?"

759
01:04:02,000 --> 01:04:08,000
Hiyori: "That's right! You just reach out and help yourself to whatever you want, like this."

760
01:04:08,000 --> 01:04:15,000
*Hiyori picks a few bits of boiled sweet potato out of the hotpot, then deposits them in Ena's bowl.*

761
01:04:15,000 --> 01:04:25,000
Hiyori: "They should be good to eat now, though you might want to wait for them to cool down. They just came out of the pot, so they're probably pretty..."

762
01:04:25,000 --> 01:04:26,000
Ena: "Ow!"

763
01:04:26,000 --> 01:04:28,000
Hiyori: "...hot, I was going to say."

764
01:04:28,000 --> 01:04:32,000
*Hiyori smiles at Ena indulgently, as a parent might.*

765
01:04:32,000 --> 01:04:40,000
*Ena, meanwhile, is busy fanning her mouth with one hand. Her amber eyes are wide with shock, and her face is flushed.*

766
01:04:40,000 --> 01:04:43,000
*I guess she must have burned her tongue.*

767
01:04:43,000 --> 01:04:49,000
*She might be particularly sensitive to shifts in the temperature, being an alien.*

768
01:04:49,000 --> 01:04:53,000
*I wonder what the weather is like on her home planet...?*

769
01:04:53,000 --> 01:04:57,000
Hiyori: "Are you alright, Ena? Do you need something to drink?"

770
01:04:57,000 --> 01:05:01,000
Hiyori: "I can pour you a cup of barley tea, if you'd like!"

771
01:05:01,000 --> 01:05:02,000
Ena: "O-Oh, no..."

772
01:05:02,000 --> 01:05:09,000
*Ena swallows her mouthful of searingly hot sweet potato, then offers Hiyori a smile of reassurance.*

773
01:05:09,000 --> 01:05:13,000
Ena: "I am quite alright. Thank you for your concern."

774
01:05:13,000 --> 01:05:18,000
Ena: "I did not expect this so-called "hotpot" to be quite so... Well, hot."

775
01:05:18,000 --> 01:05:19,000
Haru: "Really, now?"

776
01:05:19,000 --> 01:05:20,000
*I raise an eyebrow.*

777
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:22,000
Haru: "The clue is in the name."

778
01:05:22,000 --> 01:05:27,000
Ena: "The heat is not unbearable! I was simply taken by surprise, that is all."

779
01:05:27,000 --> 01:05:30,000
Ena: "My tongue does feel rather funny now, though."

780
01:05:30,000 --> 01:05:40,000
Ena: "I believe I shall follow your advice next time, and blow on my food before I put it inside my mouth. That should prevent any further mishaps!"

781
01:05:40,000 --> 01:05:43,000
Hiyori: "I do hope so. I wouldn't want to hurt you!"

782
01:05:43,000 --> 01:05:49,000
Hiyori: "Hotpot is something you're meant to enjoy, even if it does make your mouth tingle!"

783
01:05:49,000 --> 01:05:56,000
*Hiyori takes a disc of sweet potato from her own bowl and blows on it. Then, she pops it inside her own mouth.*

784
01:05:56,000 --> 01:06:00,000
*She chews for a few moments, savoring it, then sighs happily.*

785
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:05,000
Hiyori: "Now, that really is good! There's nothing I love more than sweet potato!"

786
01:06:05,000 --> 01:06:09,000
Hiyori: "I think I might like it even more than beef, ehehe~"

787
01:06:09,000 --> 01:06:12,000
Hiyori: "What about you, Ena? Do you like it?"

788
01:06:12,000 --> 01:06:19,000
Ena: "Oh, yes! This food is quite lovely! It is nothing at all like anything I have had on my home planet!"

789
01:06:19,000 --> 01:06:26,000
Hiyori: "I'm happy to hear it! Try some cabbage next, and some of the sticky rice cake Haru likes so much..."

790
01:06:26,000 --> 01:06:30,000
Hiyori: "Oh, and the beef! It should be done by now!"

791
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:38,000
*Hiyori picks out more choice items from the bubbling pot with her chopsticks, then deposits them in Ena's bowl.*

792
01:06:38,000 --> 01:06:45,000
*Steam is wafting from the pot, filling the clubroom with the scent of cooking meat and vegetables.*

793
01:06:45,000 --> 01:06:54,000
*It's a heavy kind of aroma that'll linger on my clothes for days afterwards, but that's a small price to pay, given how delicious it all is.*

794
01:06:54,000 --> 01:07:00,000
*I take some beef of my own, before Hiyori can swipe the rest, and chow down on it.*

795
01:07:00,000 --> 01:07:08,000
*The meat is sliced into fine strips, so all the flavor from the broth can seep into it. It really is quite delicious.*

796
01:07:08,000 --> 01:07:13,000
*I know I complain a lot, but I'm starting to think I'm pretty fortunate that...*

797
01:07:13,000 --> 01:07:14,000
Haru: "Mm~"

798
01:07:14,000 --> 01:07:15,000
Ena: "Aaa~!"

799
01:07:15,000 --> 01:07:20,000
*Ena and I sigh almost in unison, as we both swallow mouthfuls of food.*

800
01:07:20,000 --> 01:07:30,000
Ena: "I've never tasted anything quite like this before! It is so beyond my scope of experience, I am not sure I have the words to describe it!"

801
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:35,000
Ena: "This meat is so tender and juicy, it practically melts in my mouth!"

802
01:07:35,000 --> 01:07:38,000
Ena: "It's so easy to eat, I can't stop myself!"

803
01:07:38,000 --> 01:07:43,000
*Ena plucks a piece of cabbage from her bowl next, then tries to eat it.*

804
01:07:43,000 --> 01:07:48,000
*I say she "tries", because her first attempt is a failure, as is the second.*

805
01:07:48,000 --> 01:07:56,000
*Hiyori taught Ena how to use her chopsticks while the hotpot was still boiling, but she's yet to master the art.*

806
01:07:56,000 --> 01:08:04,000
*I suppose they don't use chopsticks in Corval. Maybe they go in for knives and forks, like they do in Western countries?*

807
01:08:04,000 --> 01:08:17,000
*Ena's been fumbling with her chopsticks a lot throughout the meal. She's splashed both the table and her clothes with broth from the hotpot, but she's so focused on the meal she doesn't seem to care.*

808
01:08:17,000 --> 01:08:21,000
*I'm tempted to offer Ena some help with the chopsticks, but...*

809
01:08:21,000 --> 01:08:22,000
Ena: "There we go!"

810
01:08:22,000 --> 01:08:25,000
*The third time is, as the saying goes, the charm.*

811
01:08:25,000 --> 01:08:30,000
*Finally, Ena is able to maneuver the cabbage to her mouth without incident.*

812
01:08:30,000 --> 01:08:40,000
*She chomps down on it quickly, as though afraid it might run away from her - which, given Ena's poor track record with her chopsticks, it just might.*

813
01:08:40,000 --> 01:08:45,000
*It's a miracle she's not dropped any of her food on the floor yet.*

814
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:51,000
*She chews the cabbage, crunching it between her teeth, then sighs as she swallows it.*

815
01:08:51,000 --> 01:08:55,000
Ena: "This is good, too! It's incredibly good, in fact!"

816
01:08:55,000 --> 01:08:59,000
*...Now, that's an overreaction if ever I've seen one.*

817
01:08:59,000 --> 01:09:09,000
*I can understand Ena's enthusiasm about the beef, which is high-grade stuff, but this is only cabbage. You can buy cabbages dirt cheap at any supermarket.*

818
01:09:09,000 --> 01:09:16,000
*They're a staple of a lot of poor people's diets - but maybe they don't grow cabbages on Corval?*

819
01:09:16,000 --> 01:09:21,000
*Ena hasn't seemed familiar with any of the food simmering away in the hotpot.*

820
01:09:21,000 --> 01:09:23,000
*What does she usually eat, anyway?*

821
01:09:23,000 --> 01:09:26,000
Haru: "You're really enjoying yourself, huh?"

822
01:09:26,000 --> 01:09:27,000
Ena: "Yes, I am!"

823
01:09:27,000 --> 01:09:29,000
*Ena nods enthusiastically.*

824
01:09:29,000 --> 01:09:37,000
Ena: "This cabbage has such an interesting texture! It is very crunchy, unlike the meat! They complement one another well!"

825
01:09:37,000 --> 01:09:45,000
Ena: "All the foods in this pot are so intriguing. None of the separate elements are alike, but that adds to the fun of it!"

826
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:51,000
Ena: "These disparate ingredients all come together to create a truly enjoyable experience!"

827
01:09:51,000 --> 01:09:57,000
Hiyori: "That's part of the fun of having hotpot! It's full of all kinds of good stuff, ehehe~"

828
01:09:57,000 --> 01:10:05,000
Hiyori: "Speaking of which, we're starting to run a little low on ingredients. Do you want me to put more meat in, Haru?"

829
01:10:05,000 --> 01:10:10,000
Haru: "Sure. I still have room for more. Can I get more rice cake, too?"

830
01:10:10,000 --> 01:10:11,000
Hiyori: "Of course!"

831
01:10:11,000 --> 01:10:18,000
*Hiyori adds a few more ingredients into the bubbling hotpot, then pokes them with her chopsticks.*

832
01:10:18,000 --> 01:10:24,000
Hiyori: "It's a good thing I bought extra beef today. I had a hunch we might need it, ehehe~"

833
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:26,000
Ena: "This is so good~"

834
01:10:26,000 --> 01:10:33,000
*Ena sighs happily, as she takes a bite from the rice cake Hiyori pilfered for her a few moments earlier.*

835
01:10:33,000 --> 01:10:40,000
Ena: "This white substance is so squishy. It is very satisfying to chew. It feels so good between my teeth!"

836
01:10:40,000 --> 01:10:44,000
Ena: "Now that I have begun to eat, it seems I cannot stop!"

837
01:10:44,000 --> 01:10:48,000
Ena: "Earthling food is too good! I'm going to get addicted!"

838
01:10:48,000 --> 01:10:55,000
*Ena eyes the bubbling hotpot with eager anticipation, her face flushed with the giddy happiness of a child.*

839
01:10:55,000 --> 01:11:03,000
Ena: "I knew coming to Earth was a good idea! Your customs are so intriguing - though I cannot say much about your utensils."

840
01:11:03,000 --> 01:11:10,000
Ena: "These chopsticks are very hard to use, but I suppose that does add the challenge of it all."

841
01:11:10,000 --> 01:11:12,000
Ena: "This is so much fun!"

842
01:11:12,000 --> 01:11:14,000
*Half an hour later...*

843
01:11:14,000 --> 01:11:16,000
Ena: "Ah! That was great!"

844
01:11:16,000 --> 01:11:23,000
*Ena sighs, contented, once she's polished off her food, then sets her now-empty bowl back down on the table.*

845
01:11:23,000 --> 01:11:28,000
Ena: "My stomach is nice and full, and I feel very warm. This so-called "hotpot"-"

846
01:11:28,000 --> 01:11:32,000
Haru: "It's not "so-called". That's what it's actually called."

847
01:11:32,000 --> 01:11:36,000
Ena: "-has raised my body temperature by a good degree."

848
01:11:36,000 --> 01:11:38,000
Ena: "I feel quite comfortable!"

849
01:11:38,000 --> 01:11:45,000
Hiyori: "I'm very happy to hear that, though I think you might've made yourself a bit too comfortable, hehe."

850
01:11:45,000 --> 01:11:49,000
*Hiyori giggles, as a deep yawn forces its way from Ena's mouth.*

851
01:11:49,000 --> 01:11:51,000
Hiyori: "Are you tired?"

852
01:11:51,000 --> 01:11:59,000
Ena: "I suppose so, yes. I am not accustomed to eating so much; particularly not dense, carbohydrate-packed foods like that."

853
01:11:59,000 --> 01:12:05,000
Ena: "I believe I am in need of a rest, so my body can properly process your human cuisine."

854
01:12:05,000 --> 01:12:10,000
*Now, that sounds kind of alarming. I'm starting to worry despite myself.*

855
01:12:10,000 --> 01:12:15,000
Haru: "Are you feeling alright, Ena? The food hasn't made you feel ill, has it?"

856
01:12:15,000 --> 01:12:16,000
Ena: "Oh, darling!"

857
01:12:16,000 --> 01:12:18,000
*A wide smile captures Ena's lips.*

858
01:12:18,000 --> 01:12:20,000
Ena: "Are you concerned about me?"

859
01:12:20,000 --> 01:12:28,000
Haru: "Yeah, I guess. I mean, you are a guest, technically speaking. I'd feel bad if Hiyori and I had poisoned you..."

860
01:12:28,000 --> 01:12:36,000
Ena: "It is quite alright. Even if such an eventuality did come to pass, I would forgive you. I know you mean me no ill will."

861
01:12:36,000 --> 01:12:42,000
Ena: "You and Hiyori have been nothing but kind to me from the moment we first met."

862
01:12:42,000 --> 01:12:45,000
Ena: "That is why you are my darling-"

863
01:12:45,000 --> 01:12:50,000
*Ena winds an arm through mine, cinching our bodies close together.*

864
01:12:50,000 --> 01:12:52,000
Ena: "-and Hiyori is my best friend!"

865
01:12:52,000 --> 01:12:57,000
Hiyori: "A best friend, am I? I like the sound of that, although..."

866
01:12:57,000 --> 01:13:04,000
*Hiyori finishes stacking the dishes then pouts, her index fingers pressed together at her front.*

867
01:13:04,000 --> 01:13:13,000
Hiyori: "I'd rather be your fellow alien. I don't think I'm from Corval, but I'm sure I must hail from somewhere beyond this galaxy."

868
01:13:13,000 --> 01:13:18,000
*...Yeah, I think I'm going to ignore Hiyori's otherworldly ramblings.*

869
01:13:18,000 --> 01:13:27,000
*I have enough on my plate at the moment, what with Ena's sudden appearance. I can only handle one bona fide alien babe in my life.*

870
01:13:27,000 --> 01:13:35,000
Ena: "Fortunately, I do not think this food will cause me any serious injury, though. I only require sleep. That is all."

871
01:13:35,000 --> 01:13:43,000
Ena: "I have had quite the busy day. My escape from the palace, and my landing upon Earth, were all very exhausting!"

872
01:13:43,000 --> 01:13:45,000
Ena: "The so-called "hotpot"-"

873
01:13:45,000 --> 01:13:49,000
*Should I even bother trying to correct her at this point?*

874
01:13:49,000 --> 01:13:54,000
*If Ena weren't so good-natured, I'd almost believe she's doing this on purpose.*

875
01:13:54,000 --> 01:13:57,000
Ena: "-has finished me off, I am afraid."

876
01:13:57,000 --> 01:14:05,000
*Ena shifts away from me at long last, her hands resting demurely upon her lap, then glances about the clubroom.*

877
01:14:05,000 --> 01:14:07,000
*Smiling bashfully, she says...*

878
01:14:07,000 --> 01:14:19,000
Ena: "I would hate to be a further burden upon the pair of you, as you have already shown me excessive kindness, but you would happen to know where I might be able to pass the night?"

879
01:14:19,000 --> 01:14:25,000
Ena: "I would very much like to rest my weary head, before I fall asleep on the spot!"

880
01:14:25,000 --> 01:14:32,000
*Another yawn punctuates the end of this sentence, which adds further credence to Ena's sleepy state.*

881
01:14:32,000 --> 01:14:37,000
*Her amber eyes bead with tears, which catch on the ends of her long eyelashes.*

882
01:14:37,000 --> 01:14:41,000
*She's so noticeably tired, her head is beginning to droop.*

883
01:14:41,000 --> 01:14:48,000
*I'm afraid she really might pass out, face-first onto the table, without some kind of intervention.*

884
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:52,000
*She needs to have a lie down at the very least, but...*

885
01:14:52,000 --> 01:14:53,000
Haru: "Hmmm..."

886
01:14:53,000 --> 01:14:56,000
*What, exactly, is to be done about this situation?*

887
01:14:56,000 --> 01:15:05,000
Haru: "I guess we could take her to a hotel, but that mightn't be the best idea. She's bound to draw attention, in a get-up like that."

888
01:15:05,000 --> 01:15:15,000
Haru: "Plus, we don't know how long she'd be staying here. It's impossible to say how many days she'd need a room. That could get pretty pricey."

889
01:15:15,000 --> 01:15:22,000
Hiyori: "Oh, don't worry about the money. I can afford to put Ena up in a hotel, for however long she desires!"

890
01:15:22,000 --> 01:15:23,000
Haru: "Really?"

891
01:15:23,000 --> 01:15:24,000
*I blink.*

892
01:15:24,000 --> 01:15:27,000
Haru: "Do you have that much disposable cash?"

893
01:15:27,000 --> 01:15:35,000
Hiyori: "I don't mean to boast - that's why I don't often speak about it - but my human parents are pretty well-off."

894
01:15:35,000 --> 01:15:41,000
Hiyori: "They give me a lot of money every month, so I don't need to worry about my finances."

895
01:15:41,000 --> 01:15:47,000
Hiyori: "That's why I'm able to buy so much high-grade beef whenever we have hotpot, hehe!"

896
01:15:47,000 --> 01:15:48,000
Haru: "I see..."

897
01:15:48,000 --> 01:15:56,000
*I had wondered about that. I've always thought the hotpots we have in our teeny-tiny clubroom were suspiciously bougie.*

898
01:15:56,000 --> 01:15:57,000
*I guess I know why.*

899
01:15:57,000 --> 01:16:07,000
*Still, I had no idea Hiyori was the scion of a rich family. She doesn't act like a well-bred young lady. I've always pegged her as more of a tomboy.*

900
01:16:07,000 --> 01:16:13,000
*She doesn't wear makeup, her hair is rather plain, and her clothes are nothing fancy.*

901
01:16:13,000 --> 01:16:19,000
*I always figured Hiyori came from a decidedly middle class family like mine, but I guess not.*

902
01:16:19,000 --> 01:16:21,000
*This is quite the revelation.*

903
01:16:21,000 --> 01:16:32,000
*Now, I'm really interested in seeing what her house looks like - but there are more important matters to hand: namely, what we're to do with our resident alien girl, Ena.*

904
01:16:32,000 --> 01:16:41,000
Haru: "Even if that's the case, I wouldn't feel comfortable putting Ena up in a hotel. I can't let you foot the bill. It wouldn't be fair..."

905
01:16:41,000 --> 01:16:44,000
*I cast a pensive look in Ena's direction.*

906
01:16:44,000 --> 01:16:47,000
Haru: "And I'd rather keep an eye on her."

907
01:16:47,000 --> 01:16:53,000
Haru: "She knows so little about our culture, she needs somebody to help show her around."

908
01:16:53,000 --> 01:16:57,000
Hiyori: "Yes, I agree. A hotel wouldn't be practical."

909
01:16:57,000 --> 01:17:01,000
Haru: "Maybe we could let her stay in the clubroom...?"

910
01:17:01,000 --> 01:17:06,000
*I muse - but as soon as I broach the idea, I find myself picking holes in it.*

911
01:17:06,000 --> 01:17:15,000
Haru: "No, that's no good, either. I doubt any faculty members would stop by and find her, but if they did, she'd get into trouble."

912
01:17:15,000 --> 01:17:18,000
Haru: "She's not even a student, after all..."

913
01:17:18,000 --> 01:17:23,000
Haru: "And, even if she was, she'd need permission to stay here overnight."

914
01:17:23,000 --> 01:17:31,000
Hiyori: "There isn't a proper bed in here either, and it's rather chilly. The windows could use some more insulating."

915
01:17:31,000 --> 01:17:41,000
*Hiyori's not wrong there. This wing of the university is pretty old, as I've pontificated on at great length already, and the walls feel paper thin.*

916
01:17:41,000 --> 01:17:51,000
*Sometimes, the windowpanes rattle when it gets particularly windy, and in the winter chill air always seems to creep through gaps in the panes.*

917
01:17:51,000 --> 01:17:56,000
*I pride myself on being rational, but this building always gives me the creeps.*

918
01:17:56,000 --> 01:18:05,000
*I'd hate to spend the night here alone, assailed by the lowing of the wind. It'd be enough to stretch thin even the strongest of nerves.*

919
01:18:05,000 --> 01:18:12,000
*Ena deserves better accommodation for the night than this dilapidated room, which still smells of hotpot.*

920
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:16,000
Hiyori: "I think it would be best if I let Ena stay in my place."

921
01:18:16,000 --> 01:18:23,000
Hiyori: "I have a whole house to myself, with two spare bedrooms. There's more than enough room for Ena!"

922
01:18:23,000 --> 01:18:27,000
Hiyori: "What do you think, Ena? Do you want to stay with me?"

923
01:18:27,000 --> 01:18:38,000
Hiyori: "I can run you a nice, hot bath to wash away your fatigue, and then we can spend the night talking about your home planet! I would love to hear all about it!"

924
01:18:38,000 --> 01:18:45,000
Hiyori: "As an alien myself, we must have an awful lot in common! We can be just like big sisters!"

925
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:50,000
Hiyori: "We can braid one another's hair, and watch movies, and eat snacks..."

926
01:18:50,000 --> 01:18:59,000
Hiyori: "And then, next morning, I can make you a delicious breakfast. I enjoy cooking a lot, in case you couldn't tell, ehehe."

927
01:18:59,000 --> 01:19:05,000
Hiyori: "Hotpot is my specialty, but I'm good at making fried fish and miso soup, too!"

928
01:19:05,000 --> 01:19:10,000
Hiyori: "I'd love to show you what a traditional Japanese breakfast is like!"

929
01:19:10,000 --> 01:19:21,000
*I can see Hiyori's getting excited by the prospect of having a girl friend about the house. Her eyes are sparkling, just like constellations in the night sky.*

930
01:19:21,000 --> 01:19:25,000
*I think this is a pretty good deal, if I do say so myself.*

931
01:19:25,000 --> 01:19:34,000
*I wouldn't go in for the hair braiding, personally, but I wouldn't turn down a chance to eat a breakfast made by Hiyori's hands.*

932
01:19:34,000 --> 01:19:39,000
*I can't see anything at all awry about Hiyori's offer, but to my surprise...*

933
01:19:39,000 --> 01:19:49,000
Ena: "That is alright, but do not concern yourself overly so with my welfare. I would not wish for you to go out of your way to accommodate me."

934
01:19:49,000 --> 01:19:58,000
Ena: "While these activities do sound fun, I fear I am in no fit state to engage in anything too intense. Your itinerary would exhaust me!"

935
01:19:58,000 --> 01:20:01,000
Ena: "I feel tired simply thinking about it!"

936
01:20:01,000 --> 01:20:02,000
Hiyori: "Oh, I see..."

937
01:20:02,000 --> 01:20:08,000
*Hiyori's shoulders slump. Pouting, she fiddles with the sleeves of her pink sweater.*

938
01:20:08,000 --> 01:20:11,000
Hiyori: "Don't you want to stay with me?"

939
01:20:11,000 --> 01:20:14,000
Ena: "Maybe I will, in the future, but for now..."

940
01:20:14,000 --> 01:20:17,000
*Ena glances at me, her eyes half-lidded.*

941
01:20:17,000 --> 01:20:23,000
Ena: "Would it be alright if I passed my first night upon this planet with you, darling?"

942
01:20:23,000 --> 01:20:24,000
Haru: "With me?"

943
01:20:24,000 --> 01:20:25,000
*Ena nods.*

944
01:20:25,000 --> 01:20:32,000
Ena: "I have grown very fond of you, and I am afraid I would not be able to sleep without you by my side."

945
01:20:32,000 --> 01:20:33,000
Haru: "Well, uh..."

946
01:20:33,000 --> 01:20:36,000
*I run a hand through my hair, abashed.*

947
01:20:36,000 --> 01:20:47,000
*This is the first time a girl's invited herself over to my flat before. Not even Hiyori is so brazen. I'm flattered, but it's all so sudden it's left me somewhat stunned.*

948
01:20:47,000 --> 01:20:53,000
Haru: "I-I'm glad you trust me so much, Ena, but that seems a little... I don't know."

949
01:20:53,000 --> 01:20:55,000
Haru: "I am a guy, you know."

950
01:20:55,000 --> 01:20:59,000
Ena: "I am aware you are a male of the human species, yes."

951
01:20:59,000 --> 01:21:01,000
Haru: "And you're a girl..."

952
01:21:01,000 --> 01:21:08,000
Ena: "I am, indeed, a female of the Corven species. That cannot be denied - but why should it matter?"

953
01:21:08,000 --> 01:21:18,000
Haru: "It matters because guys and girls don't usually spend the night together; not when they've known one another for so little time. It's inappropriate."

954
01:21:18,000 --> 01:21:19,000
Ena: "How is it?"

955
01:21:19,000 --> 01:21:20,000
*Ena frowns.*

956
01:21:20,000 --> 01:21:24,000
Ena: "You are not a stranger, darling. You are my future husband."

957
01:21:24,000 --> 01:21:33,000
Ena: "We will be spending a lot of time together soon, as a matter of course, so we must first get used to one another's company."

958
01:21:33,000 --> 01:21:35,000
Ena: "That is only logical!"

959
01:21:35,000 --> 01:21:40,000
Haru: "I don't know about that. This is all moving pretty quickly..."

960
01:21:40,000 --> 01:21:45,000
Haru: "You really would be better off with Hiyori. She'll take good care of you."

961
01:21:45,000 --> 01:21:56,000
Haru: "She's a great cook - you said you liked her hotpot, didn't you? - and it sounds like she lives in a huge house. You can have a whole room to yourself!"

962
01:21:56,000 --> 01:22:03,000
Haru: "I, meanwhile, live in this cruddy little apartment. Only guys live there, and they're a little weird..."

963
01:22:03,000 --> 01:22:04,000
Ena: "Weird?"

964
01:22:04,000 --> 01:22:06,000
*Ena inclines her head.*

965
01:22:06,000 --> 01:22:07,000
Ena: "How so?"

966
01:22:07,000 --> 01:22:16,000
Haru: "They get, uh, kind of jealous. If they see me with a girl, they might just lose it: Kosuke especially. I don't want him beating me up."

967
01:22:16,000 --> 01:22:19,000
Hiyori: "Goodness! Would Kosuke do such a thing?"

968
01:22:19,000 --> 01:22:22,000
Haru: "I dunno. I wouldn't put it past him."

969
01:22:22,000 --> 01:22:30,000
Ena: "If this "Kosuke" does hurt you, I will hurt him in return! I will not let anybody lay a finger upon you, darling!"

970
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:32,000
Haru: "...Right. Uh..."

971
01:22:32,000 --> 01:22:43,000
*I look Ena up and down. She doesn't seem all that powerful, what with her willowy limbs, but maybe she has shores of hidden strength in that slender body of hers?*

972
01:22:43,000 --> 01:22:44,000
*It is a mystery.*

973
01:22:44,000 --> 01:22:52,000
Haru: "Putting that aside, my apartment's nothing special. I don't think it'd be up to snuff for a princess like you."

974
01:22:52,000 --> 01:22:57,000
Haru: "There's only a couple of rooms, and you'll have to sleep on a futon, and-"

975
01:22:57,000 --> 01:22:59,000
Ena: "That is alright."

976
01:22:59,000 --> 01:23:03,000
*Ena cuts me off, then shifts close to me upon the couch.*

977
01:23:03,000 --> 01:23:10,000
*She presses her hands to my chest, her fingers curling in on themselves, and looks up at me winsomely.*

978
01:23:10,000 --> 01:23:11,000
*Our eyes meet.*

979
01:23:11,000 --> 01:23:15,000
*Ena blinks, her lashes trembling, and says softly...*

980
01:23:15,000 --> 01:23:27,000
Ena: "I have grown tired of luxury, having lived in a palace all my life. A change of scenery would be appreciated, and I would be willing to put up with any discomfort for your sake."

981
01:23:27,000 --> 01:23:29,000
Ena: "Please, darling..."

982
01:23:29,000 --> 01:23:35,000
*Ena leans in closer still, until I can feel her warm breath brushing against my cheek.*

983
01:23:35,000 --> 01:23:43,000
Ena: "Do not push me away. You are the first human I met when first I arrived upon this planet. That must count for something."

984
01:23:43,000 --> 01:23:45,000
Ena: "Do we not have a connection?"

985
01:23:45,000 --> 01:23:46,000
*I sigh.*

986
01:23:46,000 --> 01:23:50,000
*This situation is rather awkward, to say the least.*

987
01:23:50,000 --> 01:23:56,000
*I wish Ena wasn't so insistent, but I think I understand where she's coming from.*

988
01:23:56,000 --> 01:24:03,000
*This is her first night spent upon this planet. She doesn't know much about humans, but she does know me.*

989
01:24:03,000 --> 01:24:13,000
*She's decided she can trust me, after I (inadvertently) broke her fall during her descent, and now she refuses to spend time with anybody else.*

990
01:24:13,000 --> 01:24:18,000
*She's gotten herself rather attached, like a baby gosling to their mother.*

991
01:24:18,000 --> 01:24:22,000
*Part of me does think this is cute, but therein lies a problem.*

992
01:24:22,000 --> 01:24:32,000
*I am a guy, and Ena is a girl. She's a very pretty girl, in fact, clad in a skintight outfit, and she seems determined to make me her husband.*

993
01:24:32,000 --> 01:24:40,000
*I'm afraid, if we spend too much time together, my mind will begin to overheat from various... fantasies, shall we say.*

994
01:24:40,000 --> 01:24:45,000
*Spending a night with Ena, in my cramped apartment, would be akin to torture.*

995
01:24:45,000 --> 01:24:53,000
*She might be blissfully unaware of what effect her close proximity is having upon my body, but it's weighing down on me.*

996
01:24:53,000 --> 01:24:58,000
*I don't know if I'm mature enough to handle this situation, but...*

997
01:24:58,000 --> 01:25:01,000
Haru: "Are you sure you want to stay with me?"

998
01:25:01,000 --> 01:25:03,000
Ena: "I am 100%% positive."

999
01:25:03,000 --> 01:25:05,000
Haru: "I can't change your mind?"

1000
01:25:05,000 --> 01:25:07,000
Ena: "Not even by 1%%."

1001
01:25:07,000 --> 01:25:10,000
Haru: "And you aren't tempted by Hiyori's cooking?"

1002
01:25:10,000 --> 01:25:18,000
Ena: "It is quite the enticing proposition... But, no! I must remain strong, for the sake of our future marriage!"

1003
01:25:18,000 --> 01:25:25,000
Ena: "It would not do for me to sleep under the roof of another; not after I proposed to you, darling!"

1004
01:25:25,000 --> 01:25:32,000
Haru: "It was a one-sided proposal. I never reciprocated. I'm still not sure about this marriage thing, but..."

1005
01:25:32,000 --> 01:25:35,000
*I glance over Ena's shoulder to Hiyori.*

1006
01:25:35,000 --> 01:25:38,000
Haru: "What do you think about all of this?"

1007
01:25:38,000 --> 01:25:48,000
Hiyori: "I think it'd be more sensible if Ena stayed with me. I'm sure I have more space, and the means to look after her - but she seems attached to you."

1008
01:25:48,000 --> 01:25:49,000
*Hiyori giggles.*

1009
01:25:49,000 --> 01:25:53,000
Hiyori: "I'd feel guilty if I forced you to come along with me."

1010
01:25:53,000 --> 01:25:58,000
Hiyori: "As Ena is our guest, I think we should let her do what she wants."

1011
01:25:58,000 --> 01:25:59,000
Ena: "I concur!"

1012
01:25:59,000 --> 01:26:03,000
*Ena nods eagerly, her hair shifting about her shoulders.*

1013
01:26:03,000 --> 01:26:10,000
Ena: "I should be allowed to do what I want, as a guest - and, for tonight, at least, I want to stay with you!"

1014
01:26:10,000 --> 01:26:17,000
*Ena says "for tonight, at least", but I have a sinking feeling things won't work out that simply.*

1015
01:26:17,000 --> 01:26:26,000
*Knowing Ena (not that I do; not all that well), she'll get attached to my apartment, cruddy though it is, and then she won't want to leave.*

1016
01:26:26,000 --> 01:26:34,000
*She'll stay there for days - maybe even weeks, or months - until she tires of this planet, and I'll have to look out for her.*

1017
01:26:34,000 --> 01:26:36,000
*I'll have to cook for her, too.*

1018
01:26:36,000 --> 01:26:39,000
*My cooking is nowhere near as good as Hiyori's.*

1019
01:26:39,000 --> 01:26:42,000
*Ena's losing out, but she doesn't seem to care.*

1020
01:26:42,000 --> 01:26:47,000
*Hiyori, to my surprise, doesn't seem to care all that much either.*

1021
01:26:47,000 --> 01:26:52,000
*I thought she'd be less approving of this arrangement than she is.*

1022
01:26:52,000 --> 01:27:01,000
*She really is too nice for her own good - or maybe she's simply too pure to know what could go down, as a result of this arrangement.*

1023
01:27:01,000 --> 01:27:06,000
*Either way, she betrayed me. I've got no allies left in this fight.*

1024
01:27:06,000 --> 01:27:15,000
*I tried to do the right thing - really, I did! - but it's two against one. I can't keep arguing; not against Ena's puppy dog eyes.*

1025
01:27:15,000 --> 01:27:17,000
*I'm not happy about this, but...*

1026
01:27:17,000 --> 01:27:18,000
Haru: "Alright, fine."

1027
01:27:18,000 --> 01:27:20,000
*I capitulate, after a pause.*

1028
01:27:20,000 --> 01:27:22,000
Haru: "You can stay with me."

1029
01:27:22,000 --> 01:27:23,000
Ena: "Yay!"

1030
01:27:23,000 --> 01:27:27,000
*Ena exclaims cheerily, her chest pushed up against mine.*

1031
01:27:27,000 --> 01:27:33,000
Ena: "Thank you, darling! I knew I could rely on you! You really are a wonderful human!"

1032
01:27:33,000 --> 01:27:38,000
Hiyori: "Haru is rather wonderful, isn't he? I am partial to him myself, ehehe~"

1033
01:27:38,000 --> 01:27:42,000
Haru: "Thanks for the vote of confidence, guys. Um..."

1034
01:27:42,000 --> 01:27:49,000
*I glance away, trying (and failing) not to focus on the warm, soft sensation pushed up immodestly against me.*

1035
01:27:49,000 --> 01:27:55,000
*Ena's chest is rather big, and that skintight suit of hers is doing nothing to cover her goods.*

1036
01:27:55,000 --> 01:28:03,000
Haru: "Your outfit isn't really appropriate for wandering the streets, though, Ena. You'll get a lot of curious stares."

1037
01:28:03,000 --> 01:28:04,000
Ena: "Really?"

1038
01:28:04,000 --> 01:28:06,000
*Ena tilts her head to one side.*

1039
01:28:06,000 --> 01:28:07,000
Ena: "Why is that?"

1040
01:28:07,000 --> 01:28:10,000
Haru: "It's, uh, showing a lot of skin..."

1041
01:28:10,000 --> 01:28:14,000
Ena: "Is it? I thought my attire was rather modest myself."

1042
01:28:14,000 --> 01:28:23,000
Ena: "It is common from people who hail from Corval to wear much less! It is a hot planet, and too many layers can be awfully uncomfortable."

1043
01:28:23,000 --> 01:28:31,000
Haru: "Maybe that's true on Corval, but this is Earth. People tend not to dress like that, unless they're cosplaying."

1044
01:28:31,000 --> 01:28:36,000
Haru: "I think we'll need to get you some new clothes, if you want to blend in."

1045
01:28:36,000 --> 01:28:38,000
Haru: "What do you say, Hiyori?"

1046
01:28:38,000 --> 01:28:41,000
Hiyori: "That sounds like a good idea to me, ehehe."

1047
01:28:41,000 --> 01:28:42,000
*Hiyori giggles.*

1048
01:28:42,000 --> 01:28:49,000
Hiyori: "Luckily, it's Saturday tomorrow. We can meet up and go shopping together, if you'd like?"

1049
01:28:49,000 --> 01:28:54,000
Hiyori: "We can also show Ena around. I think she might enjoy that!"

1050
01:28:54,000 --> 01:28:55,000
Ena: "Ooh, yes!"

1051
01:28:55,000 --> 01:29:01,000
*Ena draws away from me, at long last, then beams brightly, hands clasped at her front.*

1052
01:29:01,000 --> 01:29:08,000
Ena: "I would enjoy that very much! I am most curious about this planet! I want to explore every inch of it!"

1053
01:29:08,000 --> 01:29:16,000
Hiyori: "Exploring "every inch" of Earth might be a bit much, but we can certainly go to Shinjuku, and maybe Shibuya!"

1054
01:29:16,000 --> 01:29:25,000
Hiyori: "I'm sure we'll be able to pick out a lot of adorable outfits for you, Ena! You're so pretty, you'll look good in anything!"

1055
01:29:25,000 --> 01:29:27,000
Ena: "Wonderful! I cannot wait!"

1056
01:29:27,000 --> 01:29:28,000
Ena: "Aaah~"

1057
01:29:28,000 --> 01:29:31,000
*Ena sighs, her palms pressed against her cheeks.*

1058
01:29:31,000 --> 01:29:41,000
Ena: "I am so glad I landed upon this planet. The people are so nice, the food is delicious, and tomorrow I shall explore it to my heart's content!"

1059
01:29:41,000 --> 01:29:43,000
Ena: "I really am lucky!"

1060
01:29:43,000 --> 01:29:47,000
Ena: "Ooh! Is this your abode, Haru? It is awfully cozy!"

1061
01:29:47,000 --> 01:29:55,000
Haru: "Yeah, I guess you could call it that. I wasn't born here, but it's been my home since I enrolled at university."

1062
01:29:55,000 --> 01:29:56,000
Ena: "Ah, yes."

1063
01:29:56,000 --> 01:30:01,000
*Ena glances about my room, her snub nose twitching like a rabbit's.*

1064
01:30:01,000 --> 01:30:03,000
*She isn't smelling my room, is she?*

1065
01:30:03,000 --> 01:30:06,000
*If so, that'd be kind of embarrassing...*

1066
01:30:06,000 --> 01:30:12,000
Ena: "I can tell that this residence belongs to you. It has your scent all over it."

1067
01:30:12,000 --> 01:30:21,000
*...Well, I guess that confirms both my suspicions. Ena was, indeed, sniffing my room, and this revelation is, in fact, embarrassing.*

1068
01:30:21,000 --> 01:30:31,000
*I feel my cheeks turning red, which seems to be a common occurrence around Ena. Her skimpy outfit makes it hard to know where I should be placing my eyes.*

1069
01:30:31,000 --> 01:30:35,000
*Simply being around her makes me feel like a creep.*

1070
01:30:35,000 --> 01:30:38,000
Haru: "I, uh, am sorry to hear that, I guess?"

1071
01:30:38,000 --> 01:30:42,000
*I murmur, while running a hand through my flyaway hair.*

1072
01:30:42,000 --> 01:30:44,000
Haru: "I hope that isn't a problem?"

1073
01:30:44,000 --> 01:30:52,000
Ena: "Oh, no! It's quite alright! I am glad that this room smells of you. It makes it feel more familiar, somehow."

1074
01:30:52,000 --> 01:30:58,000
Haru: "Easy there, tiger. You've only known me for a few hours. Don't get too attached."

1075
01:30:58,000 --> 01:31:06,000
Ena: "I am aware, indeed, but I would very much like to get to know you better! I think we have a real connection, you and I!"

1076
01:31:06,000 --> 01:31:11,000
Haru: "Because you crash-landed on me back on the university's roof?"

1077
01:31:11,000 --> 01:31:24,000
Ena: "That's right! There are billions of people upon this planet, or so I have heard, yet it was upon you that I fell. Our encounter was most serendipitous. I think that must count for something!"

1078
01:31:24,000 --> 01:31:28,000
Ena: "We were fated to be together. It is written in the stars!"

1079
01:31:28,000 --> 01:31:30,000
Haru: "In the stars, huh...?"

1080
01:31:30,000 --> 01:31:36,000
*I'm an astronomer myself, but that sounds like some new age mumbo-jumbo if ever I've heard it.*

1081
01:31:36,000 --> 01:31:44,000
*I didn't think Ena, being an actual alien from actual space, would be interested in horoscopes. Maybe I was mistaken.*

1082
01:31:44,000 --> 01:31:47,000
*Do they even have horoscopes on her planet?*

1083
01:31:47,000 --> 01:31:57,000
*I've no idea, but there must be some crossover between Corval and Earth's customs. Alien though she is, Ena doesn't feel like an extraterrestrial.*

1084
01:31:57,000 --> 01:32:05,000
*If it weren't for her strange attire, coupled with her strange turns of phrase, I'd think her an ordinary girl, just like...*

1085
01:32:05,000 --> 01:32:12,000
*Well, maybe not quite like Hiyori, who isn't all that normal herself, but like any of my other classmates.*

1086
01:32:12,000 --> 01:32:21,000
Ena: "I wish to familiarize myself with your planet, and with its culture. With some luck, that should bring me even closer to you, darling!"

1087
01:32:21,000 --> 01:32:24,000
Haru: "Wow, uh... You sure are enthused, huh?"

1088
01:32:24,000 --> 01:32:31,000
Ena: "Oh, yes. When I set my mind to something, I give it my all! I am being very, very earnest right now!"

1089
01:32:31,000 --> 01:32:38,000
Haru: "I'm, uh, glad to hear it, I guess. It seems like you know quite a bit about Earth already, though."

1090
01:32:38,000 --> 01:32:48,000
Ena: "I know some things, but I could always stand to discover more. I wish to participate in your culture, and involve myself in your daily life!"

1091
01:32:48,000 --> 01:32:52,000
Ena: "I'm very interested in your planet, and in you, darling!"

1092
01:32:52,000 --> 01:32:57,000
Haru: "Yeah, I figured as much. You've not been exactly subtle on that score."

1093
01:32:57,000 --> 01:33:03,000
Haru: "You're doing a pretty good job at integrating, too. I mean, you are in my room."

1094
01:33:03,000 --> 01:33:14,000
Ena: "Yes, I suppose I am. My first few hours upon this planet have gone better than even I could have anticipated, and I have always been an optimist at heart!"

1095
01:33:14,000 --> 01:33:18,000
Ena: "I am so fortunate that I ran into a kind man like you!"

1096
01:33:18,000 --> 01:33:26,000
Ena: "Though I know little of your species, I doubt many would be willing to let a stranger like me stay with them."

1097
01:33:26,000 --> 01:33:31,000
Ena: "This proves my earlier hypothesis. You really are a good person."

1098
01:33:31,000 --> 01:33:33,000
Haru: "Nah. I'm just a pushover."

1099
01:33:33,000 --> 01:33:36,000
Ena: "You are selling yourself short!"

1100
01:33:36,000 --> 01:33:42,000
*Ena stabs a finger in my direction, her pale green tresses shifting about her shoulders.*

1101
01:33:42,000 --> 01:33:49,000
Ena: "You are nice! That cannot be contested! I believe it wholeheartedly, based upon your actions..."

1102
01:33:49,000 --> 01:33:52,000
*Ena sniffs again, her nostrils quivering.*

1103
01:33:52,000 --> 01:33:54,000
Ena: "...and upon your scent."

1104
01:33:54,000 --> 01:33:57,000
*So, we're back to my smell again, are we?*

1105
01:33:57,000 --> 01:34:01,000
*Does this girl share some of her DNA with a bloodhound?*

1106
01:34:01,000 --> 01:34:09,000
*Now I'm getting self-conscious - and I was already pretty self-conscious, given Ena's scantily-clad presence in my bedroom.*

1107
01:34:09,000 --> 01:34:13,000
Haru: "This is the second time you've mentioned that..."

1108
01:34:13,000 --> 01:34:14,000
*I frown.*

1109
01:34:14,000 --> 01:34:17,000
Haru: "Are you trying to say that I smell?"

1110
01:34:17,000 --> 01:34:23,000
Ena: "You do, yes, but it is not an unpleasant smell. I have grown very fond of it!"

1111
01:34:23,000 --> 01:34:24,000
Ena: "Aaaah..."

1112
01:34:24,000 --> 01:34:28,000
*Ena inhales deeply, her long eyelashes falling shut.*

1113
01:34:28,000 --> 01:34:30,000
Ena: "I feel so relaxed!"

1114
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:32,000
Haru: "I'm glad one of us does."

1115
01:34:32,000 --> 01:34:36,000
*I've been on edge ever since Ena and I left the campus.*

1116
01:34:36,000 --> 01:34:48,000
*I was exceedingly anxious, during our trek back to my apartment, about running into any passers-by. They almost certainly would have been suspicious, given Ena's appearance.*

1117
01:34:48,000 --> 01:34:55,000
*I did lend Ena my coat during our walk, to cover her up, but I could hardly let her borrow my shoes.*

1118
01:34:55,000 --> 01:35:05,000
*She had to traipse back barefoot - which, to my surprise, didn't seem to bother her. At the very least, she showed no outwards signs of discomfort.*

1119
01:35:05,000 --> 01:35:12,000
*Maybe the soles of Corvans, or whatever her people are called, are made of tougher stuff than human soles?*

1120
01:35:12,000 --> 01:35:15,000
*I wonder if she's particularly ticklish.*

1121
01:35:15,000 --> 01:35:18,000
*That might be something to test out...*

1122
01:35:18,000 --> 01:35:20,000
*But, no, I'm getting distracted.*

1123
01:35:20,000 --> 01:35:27,000
*Speaking of distractions, Ena was awfully taken by all the sights we passed during our walk back.*

1124
01:35:27,000 --> 01:35:34,000
*She stopped to stare at every little thing which took her fancy, which reduced our pace to a snail's crawl.*

1125
01:35:34,000 --> 01:35:42,000
*I've never seen anybody gush over a vending machine before. I didn't know such a thing was possible, but Ena managed it.*

1126
01:35:42,000 --> 01:35:44,000
*Tonight has been full of surprises.*

1127
01:35:44,000 --> 01:35:51,000
*It's a further miracle I didn't alert any of my housemates when bundling Ena inside the apartment.*

1128
01:35:51,000 --> 01:35:57,000
*Trying to explain her presence away to Koichi and the others would've been a nightmare.*

1129
01:35:57,000 --> 01:36:05,000
*I'll probably have to face them at some point, though. If Ena means to stay here, she'll definitely end up running into them.*

1130
01:36:05,000 --> 01:36:17,000
*My apartment is small and old, and the walls are thin. Noise travels down the hallway with ease. It'd be impossible to hide a pet hamster in here, undetected, let alone a girl.*

1131
01:36:17,000 --> 01:36:20,000
*Thinking about it is enough to give me a headache.*

1132
01:36:20,000 --> 01:36:22,000
*I can't help but feel anxious...*

1133
01:36:22,000 --> 01:36:27,000
*But, oh well. These are problems for the me of the future to worry about.*

1134
01:36:27,000 --> 01:36:30,000
*Right now, I have more pressing concerns.*

1135
01:36:30,000 --> 01:36:36,000
Ena: "Ah, yes. This flooring beneath my feet feels so good. It's very refreshing, ehehe~"

1136
01:36:36,000 --> 01:36:42,000
Ena: "I believe I have heard it said that such flooring is called "tatami", in your country?"

1137
